WEBVTT

1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,000

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000

3
00:01:45,166 --> 00:01:46,254
<i>Listen.</i>

4
00:01:46,255 --> 00:01:47,601
<i>Don't make the same mistake again.</i>

5
00:01:48,519 --> 00:01:51,466
<i>Don't leave until you've made sure
whether he's dead or alive.</i>

6
00:02:21,286 --> 00:02:23,876
<i>♪ Slithering with the night... ♪</i>

7
00:02:24,931 --> 00:02:26,821
<i>♪ A shadow-serpent ♪</i>

8
00:02:27,278 --> 00:02:29,410
<i>♪ The world... ♪</i>

9
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,906
<i>♪ An enigma ♪</i>

10
00:02:33,399 --> 00:02:35,241
<i>♪ Upon the tongue ♪</i>

11
00:02:35,361 --> 00:02:36,763
<i>♪ Trembling... ♪</i>

12
00:02:36,913 --> 00:02:39,038
<i>♪ A fleeting moth ♪</i>

13
00:02:39,418 --> 00:02:41,258
<i>♪ Startled ♪</i>

14
00:02:43,199 --> 00:02:46,373
<i>♪ And unaware ♪</i>

15
00:02:47,569 --> 00:02:51,667
<i>♪ Clawing the soul... ♪</i>

16
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:54,867
<i>♪ Like a ploughing ox ♪</i>

17
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:57,095
<i>♪ Like a straining, ploughing ox ♪</i>

18
00:02:57,336 --> 00:02:59,307
<i>♪ Through hidden nerves... ♪</i>

19
00:02:59,308 --> 00:03:02,370
<i>♪ We'll carve our way ♪</i>

20
00:03:10,483 --> 00:03:14,038
<i>♪ Through unseen crevices... ♪</i>

21
00:03:14,039 --> 00:03:16,766
<i>♪ Let me seep into your flesh ♪</i>

22
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:19,766
<i>♪ Into skies of madness ♪</i>

23
00:03:19,767 --> 00:03:21,966
<i>♪ With newfound wings ♪</i>

24
00:03:21,967 --> 00:03:24,139
<i>♪ Like a dinosaur... ♪</i>

25
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:26,283
<i>♪ We soar! ♪</i>

26
00:03:38,284 --> 00:03:41,985
<i>♪ We manifest and shift... ♪</i>

27
00:03:42,411 --> 00:03:46,130
<i>♪ Through all things
Living and dead ♪</i>

28
00:03:51,367 --> 00:03:54,867
<i>♪ We fall and perish... ♪</i>

29
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:59,279
<i>♪ In the deep trenches of a harsh destiny ♪</i>

30
00:04:01,187 --> 00:04:05,499
<i>♪ Countless restless souls... ♪</i>

31
00:04:06,055 --> 00:04:10,110
<i>♪ In borrowed flesh ♪</i>

32
00:04:11,006 --> 00:04:13,929
<i>♪ Possessing... ♪</i>

33
00:04:14,052 --> 00:04:16,947
<i>♪ Racing in wild anxiety ♪</i>

34
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:19,486
<i>♪ We'll roam this earth... ♪</i>

35
00:04:19,487 --> 00:04:21,628
<i>♪ Forsaken! ♪</i>

36
00:04:22,448 --> 00:04:25,787
<i>♪ Broken-tailed... ♪</i>

37
00:04:27,366 --> 00:04:29,788
<i>♪ We wander! ♪</i>

38
00:04:30,657 --> 00:04:34,130
<i>♪ Through unseen truths... ♪</i>

39
00:04:34,254 --> 00:04:36,986
<i>♪ We'll crystallise at last ♪</i>

40
00:04:37,519 --> 00:04:39,708
<i>♪ Into skies of madness ♪</i>

41
00:04:39,709 --> 00:04:42,046
<i>♪ Wingless now ♪</i>

42
00:04:42,047 --> 00:04:44,001
<i>♪ Like a dinosaur... ♪</i>

43
00:04:44,002 --> 00:04:46,621
<i>♪ We'll vanish! ♪</i>

44
00:04:50,422 --> 00:04:58,320
"UNMADHAM"
(Insanity)

45
00:05:13,516 --> 00:05:14,625
<i>Roll sound...</i>

46
00:05:14,969 --> 00:05:16,258
<i>Sound rolling.</i>

47
00:05:16,758 --> 00:05:18,024
<i>Start camera.</i>

48
00:05:18,516 --> 00:05:19,766
<i>Camera rolling.</i>

49
00:05:20,188 --> 00:05:21,383
<i>Action!</i>

50
00:05:24,059 --> 00:05:25,225
Camera tilt up.

51
00:05:25,732 --> 00:05:26,732
Slowly.

52
00:05:27,924 --> 00:05:29,005
Face entry.

53
00:05:34,257 --> 00:05:35,264
Cut.

54
00:05:38,917 --> 00:05:40,177
<i>Move the van.</i>

55
00:05:52,965 --> 00:05:54,502
<i>Move that land stand.</i>

56
00:05:54,503 --> 00:05:56,416
<i>Kumar, please fix the light soon.</i>

57
00:05:56,417 --> 00:05:57,709
<i>Bring the sand bag.</i>

58
00:06:25,153 --> 00:06:26,311
Take okay.

59
00:06:26,312 --> 00:06:27,616
Sir, is this okay?

60
00:06:27,617 --> 00:06:29,205
- How's this?
- Which one?

61
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,588
It's a good story.

62
00:06:38,794 --> 00:06:40,781
But it's not really what I'm looking for.

63
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:44,627
Also, it feels a little too influenced
by English films.

64
00:06:45,767 --> 00:06:47,666
That said... your writing, the characters,

65
00:06:47,667 --> 00:06:49,416
their arcs and scenes are all really good.

66
00:06:49,417 --> 00:06:51,117
- The shot is ready.
- Alright, let's begin.

67
00:06:52,007 --> 00:06:53,375
Sir, you're in the police, right?

68
00:06:53,376 --> 00:06:55,349
If you have a good police story...

69
00:06:55,834 --> 00:06:57,181
- we can discuss it then.
- Alright.

70
00:07:10,707 --> 00:07:11,714
What happened?

71
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:13,127
Let's go.

72
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:51,201
- Go turn on the tap.
- Okay.

73
00:07:51,202 --> 00:07:52,431
You go with him too.

74
00:07:56,847 --> 00:07:58,184
Don't cry...

75
00:07:58,185 --> 00:07:59,540
It's okay, don't cry...

76
00:08:01,501 --> 00:08:02,555
You!

77
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:04,860
You still don't know how to use that?

78
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:07,157
Mom, it sprayed all over me!

79
00:08:07,158 --> 00:08:08,371
Yeah, right! Get inside.

80
00:08:08,703 --> 00:08:11,133
Soumya, the tank's empty.
Can I turn on the pump?

81
00:08:11,134 --> 00:08:12,730
Rimi, you've been sitting here all day.

82
00:08:12,731 --> 00:08:14,121
It's not like you've got a job.

83
00:08:14,122 --> 00:08:16,369
I just got back from work.
You can do it after I'm done.

84
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,418
You're the only one who goes to work.

85
00:08:18,752 --> 00:08:21,218
Someone else was home all day
without working.

86
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:27,227
- Get inside!
- Come on, run!

87
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:32,599
- Dad!
- Yes.

88
00:08:33,804 --> 00:08:36,268
A snake got into our school today.

89
00:08:36,269 --> 00:08:38,183
- Dad, today my friend...
- Let me say it.

90
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:39,439
- No, let me...
- I wanna say it!

91
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,299
- No, I wanna say it!
- Why's your uniform wet?

92
00:08:41,394 --> 00:08:43,500
Don't drip water everywhere. Go change.

93
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,193
Do I have to tell you too?

94
00:08:50,654 --> 00:08:51,812
Go on, act smart.

95
00:08:52,087 --> 00:08:53,198
You'll need me later.

96
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,327
Go on. Do it.

97
00:08:57,540 --> 00:08:58,633
How did the meeting go?

98
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:00,920
He liked my writing...

99
00:09:01,214 --> 00:09:02,802
the characters too.

100
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:04,550
But not the story.

101
00:09:05,130 --> 00:09:06,555
He asked me to write another one.

102
00:09:06,556 --> 00:09:09,227
He couldn't say your story was bad,
so he made an excuse.

103
00:09:09,562 --> 00:09:10,810
Get it now, at least.

104
00:09:10,913 --> 00:09:13,040
It's been over a year since
you stopped going to work

105
00:09:13,041 --> 00:09:14,855
and started chasing cinema
without a paycheck.

106
00:09:25,234 --> 00:09:27,987
Everyone struggles
before making it in films.

107
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,402
My father married me off
to a police officer...

108
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,012
not someone from the film industry.

109
00:09:32,786 --> 00:09:34,076
You do your films.

110
00:09:34,417 --> 00:09:35,651
Just let me go my way.

111
00:09:36,070 --> 00:09:37,609
I'll raise my kids somehow.

112
00:09:38,063 --> 00:09:39,503
I've suffered long enough.

113
00:09:40,664 --> 00:09:41,924
My dear Soumya.

114
00:09:42,224 --> 00:09:43,617
At least be kind, like your name.

115
00:09:43,704 --> 00:09:45,107
- The whole block will hear.
<i>- Rimi.</i>

116
00:09:45,108 --> 00:09:46,421
<i>I've got other work to do.</i>

117
00:09:46,422 --> 00:09:47,524
<i>Are there any more clothes?</i>

118
00:09:47,816 --> 00:09:49,243
<i>No that's it.</i>

119
00:09:49,543 --> 00:09:50,769
<i>I'll hang them out.</i>

120
00:09:50,932 --> 00:09:52,463
<i>Oh, no need. I'll also come.</i>

121
00:09:52,464 --> 00:09:53,643
Let them hear.

122
00:09:53,644 --> 00:09:55,710
I can't face anyone
in these quarters anymore.

123
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:59,035
People already blame me
for your foolishness.

124
00:09:59,806 --> 00:10:02,379
If you keep chasing films,
I'll kill the kids and kill myself.

125
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:03,933
Only then will you learn your lesson.

126
00:10:07,734 --> 00:10:09,734
- Give it here!
- No, it's mine!

127
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:11,006
Stop yelling!

128
00:10:11,007 --> 00:10:12,811
If I come there,
both of you are in trouble.

129
00:10:12,812 --> 00:10:14,456
<i>Go change your uniform.
Or she'll never stop nagging.</i>

130
00:10:14,457 --> 00:10:16,085
<i>- Go on. Get changed.
- Soumya is on fire.</i>

131
00:10:16,086 --> 00:10:17,229
<i>Shelly is too nice.</i>

132
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:21,678
I have to go to work
and do all the housework too.

133
00:10:21,907 --> 00:10:23,823
Don't know what I did to end up with you.

134
00:10:25,016 --> 00:10:26,676
<i>Rimi, any more clothes?</i>

135
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:32,258
Learn from Sumesh sir.

136
00:10:32,259 --> 00:10:33,808
- Huh?
- He goes to work...

137
00:10:34,734 --> 00:10:37,034
and still washes Rimi's undergarments
when he gets home.

138
00:10:38,702 --> 00:10:40,975
<i>That wasn't politically correct, was it?</i>

139
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:51,506
Please stop shouting.

140
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:53,387
I'll stop everything.

141
00:10:53,866 --> 00:10:55,166
I'll rejoin tomorrow.

142
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,237
If you'd tried acting instead of writing...

143
00:11:21,327 --> 00:11:22,606
you'd have won an Oscar by now.

144
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,993
I'm not asking you to stop writing.

145
00:11:36,047 --> 00:11:37,833
Can't you keep your job and write?

146
00:11:43,054 --> 00:11:44,614
Everyone downstairs is watching.

147
00:11:45,634 --> 00:11:46,640
Are they?

148
00:11:47,514 --> 00:11:49,059
Why are you all standing there?

149
00:11:49,060 --> 00:11:50,067
Is there a problem?

150
00:11:51,484 --> 00:11:53,170
Come on, let's go.

151
00:11:55,774 --> 00:11:57,462
Make sure you exercise in the morning.

152
00:11:57,463 --> 00:11:58,740
Then you do the housework, sir.

153
00:11:58,741 --> 00:12:01,107
- Were you on night duty, sir?
- Aren't you going to office?

154
00:12:02,806 --> 00:12:03,903
Get your bag, let's go.

155
00:12:03,904 --> 00:12:04,911
- Dad...
- Ready?

156
00:12:05,653 --> 00:12:06,826
- Bye.
- Okay, bye.

157
00:12:06,827 --> 00:12:08,861
If you're coming with me, get ready fast.

158
00:12:08,862 --> 00:12:10,473
I have to report at the unit by eight.

159
00:12:10,474 --> 00:12:11,884
My bike is in the workshop.

160
00:12:11,885 --> 00:12:13,577
Otherwise, I wouldn't have bothered you.

161
00:12:13,578 --> 00:12:15,285
It's not that.

162
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:17,379
I'm not used to being yelled at
like you are.

163
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:18,728
I have to get to work on time.

164
00:12:42,950 --> 00:12:44,269
That temple was in ruins.

165
00:12:44,270 --> 00:12:46,811
Menon restored it to its former glory.

166
00:12:46,812 --> 00:12:48,792
His smile shines just as bright.

167
00:12:48,898 --> 00:12:50,276
- Got any money on you?
- Huh?

168
00:13:01,747 --> 00:13:03,707
If I find out
you used it to buy cigarettes...

169
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,403
Alright.

170
00:13:09,502 --> 00:13:11,995
<i>We need more officers this time
or it'll be a mess.</i>

171
00:13:12,222 --> 00:13:13,569
<i>So many problems.</i>

172
00:13:15,667 --> 00:13:16,963
Everybody, come out.

173
00:13:17,067 --> 00:13:18,453
Look who decided to show up.

174
00:13:19,439 --> 00:13:20,546
Aha!

175
00:13:20,767 --> 00:13:21,774
What's up?

176
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:23,577
Heard Mammootty and Mohanlal quit acting

177
00:13:23,578 --> 00:13:25,480
because you didn't cast them in your film.

178
00:13:25,739 --> 00:13:26,805
What a filmmaker!

179
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:29,097
Why don't you take five years' leave?

180
00:13:29,098 --> 00:13:30,538
At least we can replace you.

181
00:13:30,539 --> 00:13:32,853
He goes on medical leave
and we've got twice the work.

182
00:13:32,854 --> 00:13:34,455
Take Sir's bag inside.

183
00:13:34,614 --> 00:13:36,313
He must've forgotten the station limits.

184
00:13:36,314 --> 00:13:37,686
Get in. Let's go for a ride.

185
00:13:37,687 --> 00:13:38,694
Come on.

186
00:13:49,507 --> 00:13:50,514
Shelly sir?

187
00:13:51,313 --> 00:13:53,192
Don't forget what I told you.

188
00:13:53,193 --> 00:13:54,200
About what?

189
00:13:55,693 --> 00:13:58,476
About getting my daughter into films.

190
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:01,036
She'll get paid more for stage shows too.

191
00:14:01,037 --> 00:14:02,512
That's why I asked him, sir.

192
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,084
He's written quite a few scripts.

193
00:14:05,353 --> 00:14:06,764
He'll surely get her a role.

194
00:14:11,613 --> 00:14:12,620
Listen, brother...

195
00:14:12,967 --> 00:14:14,687
It's true I chased films for a while.

196
00:14:14,967 --> 00:14:17,093
I really wanted it.
I tried hard but it didn't work.

197
00:14:18,369 --> 00:14:19,552
I've given it all up.

198
00:14:19,553 --> 00:14:20,560
I can't do it anymore.

199
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:23,480
For God's sake,
don't come to me with this again.

200
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:53,255
Down with the land-grabbing government!

201
00:14:53,256 --> 00:14:58,840
Resign! Step down!

202
00:14:58,937 --> 00:15:03,452
We protest! We protest!

203
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,607
Do you know...

204
00:15:22,340 --> 00:15:23,722
Back in college,

205
00:15:23,723 --> 00:15:25,190
I won Best Actor at university.

206
00:15:26,030 --> 00:15:28,169
I tried films too. Didn't work out.

207
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:31,650
There's one thing I envy about you.

208
00:15:32,277 --> 00:15:34,750
At least you're still chasing your dream.

209
00:15:50,793 --> 00:15:51,799
Sir.

210
00:15:53,213 --> 00:15:54,560
He loves doing all this.

211
00:15:54,773 --> 00:15:56,536
It's just to show off in front of you. sir.

212
00:16:23,928 --> 00:16:24,982
<i>Hello.</i>

213
00:16:25,251 --> 00:16:26,286
Where are you?

214
00:16:37,777 --> 00:16:39,557
<i>Look, I'm at the unit itself.</i>

215
00:16:40,070 --> 00:16:41,097
<i>Happy now?</i>

216
00:16:44,650 --> 00:16:46,604
I was just by the roadside.

217
00:16:46,858 --> 00:16:47,895
Thought I'd call you.

218
00:16:47,896 --> 00:16:48,963
I understood.

219
00:16:48,964 --> 00:16:50,421
Which affair did you bust today?

220
00:17:09,467 --> 00:17:10,654
Why'd you let them off, sir?

221
00:17:10,655 --> 00:17:12,599
What do we gain
by breaking up two families?

222
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,662
Get in.

223
00:17:14,107 --> 00:17:15,763
Shelly, we've got a complaint.

224
00:17:15,764 --> 00:17:18,046
Neighbour dispute. Go check it out.

225
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:19,527
- Okay, sir.
- Let's go.

226
00:17:32,197 --> 00:17:33,585
Dakshayiniamma?

227
00:17:34,343 --> 00:17:36,436
I'm Dakshayiniamma, sir.

228
00:17:36,437 --> 00:17:38,707
- There was a complaint?
- Yes, I gave the complaint.

229
00:17:38,708 --> 00:17:42,225
It's just me and
my marriageable-age daughters here.

230
00:17:42,496 --> 00:17:44,555
My husband passed away years ago.

231
00:17:44,556 --> 00:17:46,494
The old man in that house,

232
00:17:46,495 --> 00:17:48,155
comes up to this fence...

233
00:17:48,156 --> 00:17:50,327
pees here and lifts his clothes.

234
00:17:50,328 --> 00:17:51,932
My eyes can't take it anymore.

235
00:17:51,933 --> 00:17:54,214
How are my kids and I supposed to sit here?

236
00:17:54,943 --> 00:17:56,707
Sir, please go and check.

237
00:17:56,708 --> 00:17:57,747
Who else is there?

238
00:17:57,748 --> 00:17:59,335
He's got kids.

239
00:17:59,336 --> 00:18:00,742
But they are all away.

240
00:18:00,743 --> 00:18:02,355
With behaviour like that, no wonder.

241
00:18:02,356 --> 00:18:03,971
- I'll go take a look.
- Yes please do.

242
00:18:03,972 --> 00:18:04,996
- Sir...
- Hm?

243
00:18:04,997 --> 00:18:07,130
Remove that metal sheet.
You can get through there.

244
00:18:08,654 --> 00:18:10,872
- That way?
- There's a path through the trees.

245
00:18:10,873 --> 00:18:11,908
You can cross.

246
00:18:27,350 --> 00:18:29,123
Press it, sir. He's inside.

247
00:18:29,124 --> 00:18:30,350
He's definitely inside.

248
00:18:35,721 --> 00:18:38,593
Why are you going near that fence to pee?

249
00:18:38,846 --> 00:18:40,047
Only women live there.

250
00:18:40,299 --> 00:18:42,359
Sir, do I look capable of that?

251
00:18:44,782 --> 00:18:46,944
They keep stealing coconuts from my yard.

252
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:49,254
So I filed a complaint against them.

253
00:18:49,928 --> 00:18:51,707
This is payback for that.

254
00:18:54,194 --> 00:18:55,262
Oh, no...

255
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:57,897
Brother... What happened?

256
00:18:58,853 --> 00:18:59,879
Somebody help!

257
00:19:00,283 --> 00:19:01,290
Brother...

258
00:19:01,709 --> 00:19:02,716
Hey, Sister...

259
00:19:03,168 --> 00:19:04,175
Brother...

260
00:19:04,806 --> 00:19:05,813
Sister!

261
00:19:06,176 --> 00:19:08,223
- Brother, open your eyes.
- Oh, dear...

262
00:19:10,162 --> 00:19:12,190
Oh, no... He killed him!

263
00:19:15,176 --> 00:19:16,947
<i>Just because he had no one,</i>

264
00:19:16,948 --> 00:19:18,494
<i>you think you can do anything?</i>

265
00:19:18,495 --> 00:19:19,962
<i>Don't think we'll let this go.</i>

266
00:19:19,963 --> 00:19:20,987
Sir, don't argue.

267
00:19:20,988 --> 00:19:22,832
He died because that
policeman tortured him.

268
00:19:22,833 --> 00:19:25,029
The inquest is done.
There are no injuries on his body.

269
00:19:25,030 --> 00:19:26,230
You all saw that yourselves.

270
00:19:26,231 --> 00:19:27,963
Mental torture can cause a heart attack.

271
00:19:27,964 --> 00:19:29,204
You must investigate.

272
00:19:29,403 --> 00:19:31,155
Calm down. Wait for the postmortem report.

273
00:19:31,156 --> 00:19:32,190
Then we'll see.

274
00:19:32,191 --> 00:19:34,492
You can make
the postmortem report say anything.

275
00:19:34,493 --> 00:19:36,125
This is nothing new for you.

276
00:19:36,126 --> 00:19:37,903
Beating people up in custody.

277
00:19:37,904 --> 00:19:39,886
The senior officers
are trying to prevent a clash.

278
00:19:40,103 --> 00:19:41,513
What really happened, sister?

279
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:43,733
We thought he was
a community police officer

280
00:19:43,925 --> 00:19:45,485
and that he'd be polite.

281
00:19:45,721 --> 00:19:47,148
The way he questioned him...

282
00:19:47,149 --> 00:19:49,607
would've scared
even a healthy man to death.

283
00:19:49,905 --> 00:19:51,919
<i>And that poor man, what can I say...</i>

284
00:19:59,336 --> 00:20:00,343
Soumya...

285
00:20:01,417 --> 00:20:02,423
Mm?

286
00:20:05,217 --> 00:20:06,444
Don't get angry.

287
00:20:07,284 --> 00:20:08,842
I need to tell you something.

288
00:20:10,868 --> 00:20:12,193
If it's about films, don't.

289
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:13,342
I will get angry.

290
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:17,787
I might get suspended tomorrow.

291
00:20:24,267 --> 00:20:25,273
What happened?

292
00:20:37,467 --> 00:20:39,367
I went to check a complaint.

293
00:20:39,467 --> 00:20:41,227
An old man saw me, collapsed and died.

294
00:20:41,954 --> 00:20:43,053
But why suspend you?

295
00:20:43,054 --> 00:20:44,278
You didn't do anything wrong.

296
00:20:45,392 --> 00:20:47,024
They're calling it police harassment.

297
00:20:47,594 --> 00:20:49,594
The locals have formed an action council.

298
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:01,987
Didn't you say only policemen

299
00:21:02,479 --> 00:21:04,350
who work get suspended?

300
00:21:06,267 --> 00:21:07,578
Anyway, it's only six months.

301
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:10,173
You can write another story.

302
00:21:19,267 --> 00:21:20,274
Who's it?

303
00:21:23,660 --> 00:21:24,667
It's CI Sir.

304
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,407
Yes, sir?

305
00:21:29,766 --> 00:21:30,773
Sir.

306
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:34,066
Sir.

307
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:38,807
Thank you, sir.

308
00:21:39,434 --> 00:21:40,440
Sir.

309
00:21:43,620 --> 00:21:44,926
The postmortem report came.

310
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:47,166
The cause of death was kidney failure.

311
00:21:47,694 --> 00:21:48,760
So I'm cleared.

312
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:51,303
But I got a punishment transfer.

313
00:21:53,087 --> 00:21:56,153
The SP did it to pacify the action council.

314
00:21:56,674 --> 00:21:57,680
Anyway, that's good.

315
00:21:58,874 --> 00:22:01,643
At least I won't have to hear
“scriptwriter” thrown at me anymore.

316
00:22:11,687 --> 00:22:13,022
Since we're awake anyway,

317
00:22:13,553 --> 00:22:14,813
shall we go to the other room?

318
00:22:20,887 --> 00:22:21,894
Yes.

319
00:22:27,046 --> 00:22:28,786
Which station did you get transferred to?

320
00:22:29,066 --> 00:22:30,120
Kongad.

321
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:32,050
That's where your Joshy sir is, right?

322
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:33,967
Yes.

323
00:22:34,100 --> 00:22:35,490
Listen... if you team up with him

324
00:22:35,491 --> 00:22:37,453
take out a loan and make a short film...

325
00:22:37,454 --> 00:22:38,690
I swear I'll kill you.

326
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:41,273
Oh, please don't ruin the mood.

327
00:22:58,260 --> 00:23:00,299
Why weren't you answering your phone?

328
00:23:01,047 --> 00:23:02,593
I was riding my bike.

329
00:23:02,744 --> 00:23:03,790
Come.

330
00:23:04,703 --> 00:23:05,797
Hold this for a second.

331
00:23:06,108 --> 00:23:07,314
Are your father's funeral rites over?

332
00:23:07,566 --> 00:23:08,812
No.

333
00:23:09,493 --> 00:23:11,057
Who takes signed cheque leaves

334
00:23:11,058 --> 00:23:12,675
from a friend before lending money?

335
00:23:12,900 --> 00:23:14,744
Tell Sir the truth. Don't act smart.

336
00:23:15,001 --> 00:23:17,720
Sir, they handed them over themselves,
saying it was only for security.

337
00:23:17,721 --> 00:23:18,774
Let me see.

338
00:23:19,323 --> 00:23:21,612
Sir, the cheque, it's in the lady's name.

339
00:23:22,707 --> 00:23:25,124
Satheesh and his family
have been missing for a week.

340
00:23:25,637 --> 00:23:28,882
I know all about the stunt you pulled
at their house with those goons.

341
00:23:28,883 --> 00:23:31,043
If anything has happened
to Satheesh or his family...

342
00:23:31,470 --> 00:23:32,788
you'll pay for it.

343
00:23:33,166 --> 00:23:35,110
- You may leave.
- Move. Walk.

344
00:23:39,223 --> 00:23:40,657
Sir, I've come to join duty.

345
00:23:40,658 --> 00:23:42,516
- What's with the beard?
- Shaving rest, sir.

346
00:23:44,014 --> 00:23:45,053
Sir, we're from the same batch.

347
00:23:45,054 --> 00:23:46,614
Shelly has written screenplays too.

348
00:23:46,615 --> 00:23:48,437
That road safety short film I acted in,

349
00:23:48,438 --> 00:23:49,852
Shelly directed it.

350
00:23:51,833 --> 00:23:53,586
I don't want cinema people in this station.

351
00:23:53,587 --> 00:23:54,961
I need policemen who do their job.

352
00:23:55,569 --> 00:23:56,991
We're already short-staffed here.

353
00:23:56,992 --> 00:23:59,594
Don't come asking for leave
to work in films and all that.

354
00:24:01,010 --> 00:24:02,523
- Give this to the writer.
- Sir...

355
00:24:07,981 --> 00:24:12,102
For God's sake, stop advertising
my miserable film career.

356
00:24:12,259 --> 00:24:13,329
Come on, man...

357
00:24:13,595 --> 00:24:15,955
I only said it so he'd respect you.

358
00:24:17,003 --> 00:24:18,726
Yeah, I got plenty of respect.

359
00:24:18,923 --> 00:24:19,939
Give me that.

360
00:24:22,866 --> 00:24:23,913
Sir...

361
00:24:25,733 --> 00:24:27,383
Why a punishment transfer?

362
00:24:28,125 --> 00:24:30,407
A man saw me and dropped dead, sir.

363
00:24:31,075 --> 00:24:32,570
By seeing you? Really?

364
00:24:33,969 --> 00:24:35,375
Which batch are you from?

365
00:24:35,476 --> 00:24:36,944
2005 Palakkad batch.

366
00:24:36,945 --> 00:24:38,882
And you didn't write the HC test?

367
00:24:39,013 --> 00:24:40,210
No, sir.

368
00:24:40,555 --> 00:24:43,417
If you want to survive in this station,
you'd better take the next test.

369
00:24:43,418 --> 00:24:44,872
None of your tricks will work here.

370
00:24:44,873 --> 00:24:47,274
We're so short-staffed,
we can't even do the GD entries.

371
00:24:47,407 --> 00:24:49,547
Go get the bio-data register
from that cupboard.

372
00:25:03,093 --> 00:25:04,328
Sir, this one?

373
00:25:07,063 --> 00:25:08,562
Didn't I ask for that damn book?

374
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:10,743
Then why the hell did you touch that one?!

375
00:25:10,744 --> 00:25:12,250
Just to drive me crazy?

376
00:25:12,873 --> 00:25:14,235
Are you an idiot?

377
00:25:14,236 --> 00:25:15,563
Can't you recognize a book?

378
00:25:15,753 --> 00:25:17,691
We'd only just found some peace.

379
00:25:17,907 --> 00:25:20,366
Do you know what happened
to everyone who touched that file?

380
00:25:20,367 --> 00:25:22,598
We got rid of its curse
only after countless rituals.

381
00:25:22,923 --> 00:25:25,051
Do you have any idea
what's going to happen now

382
00:25:25,052 --> 00:25:26,457
- because of your stupidity?
- Sir,

383
00:25:26,458 --> 00:25:27,942
there's been
a terrible accident outside.

384
00:25:27,943 --> 00:25:30,048
Looks like the victim is dead.
My shift is already over.

385
00:25:30,049 --> 00:25:32,384
You caused this mess.
Now deal with it.

386
00:25:33,150 --> 00:25:34,326
Go!

387
00:25:35,955 --> 00:25:37,453
What are you waiting for?

388
00:25:52,821 --> 00:25:54,165
Stop crowding around here!

389
00:25:55,672 --> 00:25:56,765
Happy now?

390
00:25:56,766 --> 00:25:58,046
What a pain!

391
00:25:58,992 --> 00:26:01,121
What are you staring at? Lift him!

392
00:26:01,383 --> 00:26:03,711
He touched that file, and now he's frozen.

393
00:26:16,630 --> 00:26:18,394
Why did you touch that file?

394
00:26:19,850 --> 00:26:21,265
What did I even do?

395
00:26:22,563 --> 00:26:24,684
How was I supposed to know
what was inside it?

396
00:26:25,293 --> 00:26:27,653
Ever since I touched it,
everyone's been yelling at me.

397
00:26:29,651 --> 00:26:32,114
Six years ago, a girl was found dead
on the railway tracks.

398
00:26:32,704 --> 00:26:34,744
Since the investigation found
no signs of murder,

399
00:26:34,745 --> 00:26:36,639
the case was closed under Section 174.

400
00:26:37,486 --> 00:26:40,067
Ever since then, anyone who
touches that file lands in trouble.

401
00:26:40,375 --> 00:26:41,930
Either policemen get suspended,

402
00:26:42,454 --> 00:26:44,329
or a wave of unnatural deaths follows,

403
00:26:44,438 --> 00:26:46,313
and if not that...

404
00:26:47,188 --> 00:26:49,668
some cop's uniform in the station
ends up stained with blood.

405
00:27:11,243 --> 00:27:12,533
Rajesh, I'm leaving.

406
00:27:12,534 --> 00:27:13,813
Okay, sir

407
00:27:17,140 --> 00:27:19,840
Hey, Writer Anil sir is looking for you.

408
00:27:25,569 --> 00:27:26,718
What is it, sir?

409
00:27:26,883 --> 00:27:28,430
Another 174 case has come in.

410
00:27:28,431 --> 00:27:29,814
A four-day-old corpse.

411
00:27:30,985 --> 00:27:32,702
Shelly, there's body-watch duty.

412
00:27:32,703 --> 00:27:34,829
Take the Home Guard
and relieve the GD there.

413
00:27:34,830 --> 00:27:36,251
Someone will relieve you by morning.

414
00:27:36,252 --> 00:27:38,932
Sir, I joined only today.
I didn't even bring spare clothes.

415
00:27:39,044 --> 00:27:41,778
You're the reason for all this.
Now go stand there.

416
00:28:10,618 --> 00:28:11,830
Hold tightly.

417
00:28:11,831 --> 00:28:13,172
Tie him up!

418
00:28:17,836 --> 00:28:18,891
Sir...

419
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:21,419
The relatives and locals have all left.

420
00:28:21,420 --> 00:28:22,607
The smell here is unbearable.

421
00:28:22,608 --> 00:28:24,872
Shall we sit over there instead?
Come.

422
00:28:51,540 --> 00:28:52,602
Sir...

423
00:28:54,345 --> 00:28:55,899
What's that sound?

424
00:29:00,310 --> 00:29:02,566
The kind of duty we get
in the middle of the night!

425
00:29:04,907 --> 00:29:05,999
Sir...

426
00:29:10,351 --> 00:29:12,070
There's a loud noise inside.

427
00:29:13,064 --> 00:29:14,507
Probably a toddy cat, sir.

428
00:29:14,658 --> 00:29:15,854
Really?

429
00:29:20,294 --> 00:29:21,491
Sir...

430
00:29:23,504 --> 00:29:24,712
The smell is unbearable.

431
00:29:24,884 --> 00:29:26,667
We've run out of incense sticks.

432
00:29:26,844 --> 00:29:28,404
There are some by the porch.

433
00:29:29,323 --> 00:29:31,293
What? You want me to go to the porch?

434
00:29:52,033 --> 00:29:53,766
Sir, don't go alone, sir.

435
00:30:08,191 --> 00:30:10,364
Where did you serve in the army?

436
00:30:10,577 --> 00:30:11,830
Mostly Kashmir.

437
00:30:13,769 --> 00:30:15,503
You're scared of a dead body,

438
00:30:15,622 --> 00:30:17,340
yet you guarded the border?

439
00:30:19,650 --> 00:30:22,696
Sir, ghosts and spirits
aren't like human beings.

440
00:30:26,335 --> 00:30:28,500
Oh, come on! Ghosts, my foot!

441
00:30:30,312 --> 00:30:32,320
If there's nothing to fear,

442
00:30:32,321 --> 00:30:34,949
why are the policemen at the station
so terrified of that file?

443
00:30:34,950 --> 00:30:37,841
There was a DYSP
who talked just like you.

444
00:30:38,487 --> 00:30:40,242
Do you know what happened to him, sir?

445
00:30:40,922 --> 00:30:42,688
[police drill commands]

446
00:31:00,609 --> 00:31:02,930
How many LP warrants are pending?

447
00:31:03,103 --> 00:31:04,282
Nineteen, sir.

448
00:31:06,367 --> 00:31:09,915
Does anyone have
any duty-related grievances?

449
00:31:10,573 --> 00:31:12,132
The entire force feels

450
00:31:12,133 --> 00:31:14,046
we should conduct
a <i>puja</i> at the station.

451
00:31:14,251 --> 00:31:16,173
A <i>puja</i>? At the station?

452
00:31:16,610 --> 00:31:19,469
Sir, there's an old 174 case file here
from three years ago.

453
00:31:20,531 --> 00:31:21,938
Whenever anyone touches it,

454
00:31:21,939 --> 00:31:23,883
something unfortunate happens
at the station.

455
00:31:24,131 --> 00:31:25,715
What do you think will happen?

456
00:31:26,816 --> 00:31:28,801
Sir, officers get suspended.

457
00:31:29,042 --> 00:31:31,673
And that's not all.
The station gets flooded with 174 cases.

458
00:31:32,026 --> 00:31:34,791
At the very least, someone's uniform
ends up stained with blood.

459
00:31:35,677 --> 00:31:37,141
Aren't you ashamed?

460
00:31:37,349 --> 00:31:39,986
Dragging superstition
into the 21st century?

461
00:31:40,119 --> 00:31:42,439
People like you
don't deserve to wear that uniform.

462
00:31:42,569 --> 00:31:44,017
This isn't just my experience, sir.

463
00:31:44,018 --> 00:31:46,025
You can ask anyone here.

464
00:31:48,307 --> 00:31:49,665
Bring me that file.

465
00:31:51,702 --> 00:31:53,290
Sir, I don't think that's a good idea.

466
00:31:53,291 --> 00:31:55,102
Just bring me the file.

467
00:32:03,255 --> 00:32:04,285
Go.

468
00:32:04,286 --> 00:32:06,789
I can't touch that file today, sir.

469
00:32:08,407 --> 00:32:09,509
Daksha...

470
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:11,512
Go get that file.

471
00:32:46,393 --> 00:32:47,490
Sir...

472
00:32:47,491 --> 00:32:51,707
[Crowd chanting anti-police slogans]
Long Live IFPA! Long Live IFPA!

473
00:32:51,708 --> 00:32:55,100
<i>Beware! Beware! Beware!</i>

474
00:32:55,101 --> 00:32:57,375
<i>Police, beware!</i>

475
00:33:10,868 --> 00:33:12,816
That's the opening scene.

476
00:33:14,308 --> 00:33:15,918
The opening scene is okay.

477
00:33:16,242 --> 00:33:18,722
But where does the story go from there?

478
00:33:19,459 --> 00:33:21,389
A policeman who dreams
of becoming a screenwriter

479
00:33:21,507 --> 00:33:23,003
starts investigating this file

480
00:33:23,004 --> 00:33:25,393
and tries to turn it into a story.

481
00:33:26,893 --> 00:33:28,262
That's interesting.

482
00:33:29,006 --> 00:33:30,208
Here's what you do.

483
00:33:30,600 --> 00:33:32,217
Prepare a one-line synopsis.

484
00:33:32,792 --> 00:33:34,352
We'll build it from there.

485
00:33:36,161 --> 00:33:37,769
- Okay.
- Okay. Thank you.

486
00:33:54,312 --> 00:33:57,172
<i>♪ Far... far beyond... ♪</i>

487
00:33:57,632 --> 00:33:59,991
<i>♪ Could it be the fabled golden deer? ♪</i>

488
00:33:59,992 --> 00:34:02,632
<i>♪ Through forests no one dared to roam ♪</i>

489
00:34:02,789 --> 00:34:05,578
<i>♪ Along forbidden roads untrod ♪</i>

490
00:34:05,953 --> 00:34:08,399
<i>♪ Yet when I finally draw near ♪</i>

491
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:11,125
<i>♪ Is she a helpless orphan...
Or a formless apparition? ♪</i>

492
00:34:11,586 --> 00:34:14,289
<i>♪ Yet when I finally draw near ♪</i>

493
00:34:14,444 --> 00:34:16,929
<i>♪ Is she a helpless orphan...
Or a formless apparition? ♪</i>

494
00:34:16,930 --> 00:34:19,610
<i>♪ A tale no soul has ever spoken ♪</i>

495
00:34:19,611 --> 00:34:22,576
<i>♪ A legend no realm has ever known ♪</i>

496
00:34:22,577 --> 00:34:25,320
<i>♪ A whisper no ear has ever heard ♪</i>

497
00:34:25,321 --> 00:34:28,125
<i>♪ A phantom veiled in the folds of night ♪</i>

498
00:34:28,126 --> 00:34:31,146
<i>♪ Who knows where its roots begin
Or where its ending lies? ♪</i>

499
00:34:31,147 --> 00:34:33,772
<i>♪ Is it nothing more than
a tangled riddle? ♪</i>

500
00:34:34,126 --> 00:34:36,611
<i>♪ Far... far beyond... ♪</i>

501
00:34:37,040 --> 00:34:39,407
<i>♪ Could it be the fabled golden deer? ♪</i>

502
00:34:39,532 --> 00:34:42,204
<i>♪ Through forests no one dared to roam ♪</i>

503
00:34:42,611 --> 00:34:45,103
<i>♪ Along forbidden roads untrod ♪</i>

504
00:34:47,767 --> 00:34:49,619
The cook is waiting outside
for the payment.

505
00:34:49,620 --> 00:34:50,791
Tell him we'll pay tomorrow.

506
00:34:50,792 --> 00:34:51,993
You go tell him yourself.

507
00:34:54,337 --> 00:34:57,282
The cook doesn't know
if the society bought our paddy or not.

508
00:35:01,505 --> 00:35:03,399
After all, no one else
helps with the expenses.

509
00:35:20,946 --> 00:35:26,180
<i>♪ The season of storms
Draws its veil across every eye ♪</i>

510
00:35:26,611 --> 00:35:32,774
<i>♪ Smoke shrouds the earth
As fate quietly casts its nets ♪</i>

511
00:35:32,775 --> 00:35:37,493
<i>♪ Somewhere,
Serpents keep their timeless watch ♪</i>

512
00:35:38,376 --> 00:35:43,454
<i>♪ Is everything before us
Merely an illusion of the eye? ♪</i>

513
00:35:43,876 --> 00:35:49,009
<i>♪ Yet when I finally draw near ♪</i>

514
00:35:49,376 --> 00:35:54,736
<i>♪ Is she a helpless orphan...
Or a formless apparition? ♪</i>

515
00:35:54,829 --> 00:35:57,679
<i>♪ A tale no soul has ever spoken ♪</i>

516
00:35:57,680 --> 00:36:00,352
<i>♪ A legend no realm has ever known ♪</i>

517
00:36:00,477 --> 00:36:03,040
<i>♪ A whisper no ear has ever heard ♪</i>

518
00:36:03,041 --> 00:36:06,126
<i>♪ A phantom veiled in the folds of night ♪</i>

519
00:36:06,127 --> 00:36:09,211
<i>♪ Who knows where its roots begin
Or where its ending lies? ♪</i>

520
00:36:09,321 --> 00:36:11,695
<i>♪ Is it nothing more than
a tangled riddle? ♪</i>

521
00:36:11,696 --> 00:36:14,469
<i>♪ Far... far beyond... ♪</i>

522
00:36:14,594 --> 00:36:17,204
<i>♪ Could it be the fabled golden deer? ♪</i>

523
00:36:17,383 --> 00:36:20,102
<i>♪ Through forests no one dared to roam ♪</i>

524
00:36:20,266 --> 00:36:22,821
<i>♪ Along forbidden roads untrod ♪</i>

525
00:36:23,001 --> 00:36:24,227
Spin the swing!

526
00:36:24,228 --> 00:36:25,555
Enough?

527
00:36:25,556 --> 00:36:28,484
No, not enough. Spin it faster!

528
00:36:29,986 --> 00:36:31,767
Hey, you're in the inquest photos.

529
00:36:32,242 --> 00:36:34,883
Isn't this the suicide case
you were guarding the other day?

530
00:36:34,884 --> 00:36:36,361
It wasn't a suicide.

531
00:36:36,362 --> 00:36:38,485
Three or four people killed him over a
property dispute

532
00:36:38,486 --> 00:36:39,710
and staged it as a hanging.

533
00:36:39,711 --> 00:36:42,406
Come on! The post-mortem report says
he had cancer.

534
00:36:42,798 --> 00:36:45,430
He even left a suicide note saying
that's why he ended his life.

535
00:36:48,408 --> 00:36:50,861
No wonder none of the directors
accept your stories.

536
00:36:51,242 --> 00:36:53,374
You keep writing stories
with no logic at all.

537
00:36:55,522 --> 00:36:56,752
Come on, let's go.

538
00:36:56,753 --> 00:36:59,694
Sir isn't here. He's stepped out.
I'll check and let you know.

539
00:37:05,577 --> 00:37:06,702
Hey...

540
00:37:07,110 --> 00:37:09,194
I met Ratheesh Kumar

541
00:37:09,281 --> 00:37:11,405
and told him
about our station's 174 case file.

542
00:37:11,406 --> 00:37:12,451
Hey...

543
00:37:12,452 --> 00:37:13,757
Let me finish!

544
00:37:14,171 --> 00:37:15,320
He liked the story.

545
00:37:15,849 --> 00:37:18,111
He asked me to come back
with a one-line as soon as possible.

546
00:37:18,112 --> 00:37:20,458
Hey, that's a cursed case.
Don't get involved with it.

547
00:37:20,554 --> 00:37:23,027
Everyone who went after that file
ended up paying the price.

548
00:37:23,028 --> 00:37:25,278
- Isn't that just superstition?
- Oh, really?

549
00:37:25,631 --> 00:37:27,638
First, we need to get our hands
on that file.

550
00:37:28,849 --> 00:37:30,177
As if that'll ever happen.

551
00:37:30,282 --> 00:37:32,356
Writer Anil locks it up

552
00:37:32,357 --> 00:37:34,630
and hides the key before he leaves.

553
00:37:34,943 --> 00:37:36,537
If he finds out we touched that file,

554
00:37:36,538 --> 00:37:38,030
we're finished in this station.

555
00:37:38,031 --> 00:37:39,030
- Hey, I--
- Shelly sir,

556
00:37:39,031 --> 00:37:40,310
two people are here to see you.

557
00:37:44,257 --> 00:37:46,380
<i>Sir, we'll have only three months.</i>

558
00:37:46,381 --> 00:37:48,485
<i>So let's begin pre-production
within a month.</i>

559
00:37:48,486 --> 00:37:51,296
<i>That's fine. Sort everything out
before I leave.</i>

560
00:37:51,691 --> 00:37:52,732
<i>Will do, sir.</i>

561
00:37:53,836 --> 00:37:55,411
This is Isaac sir, the producer.

562
00:37:55,564 --> 00:37:56,751
- Hello.
- Hello.

563
00:37:57,105 --> 00:37:58,633
We've got good news.

564
00:37:58,884 --> 00:38:00,384
Sir loved your story.

565
00:38:00,969 --> 00:38:03,204
He wants the shooting to begin
within four months.

566
00:38:03,205 --> 00:38:05,273
Sir has Soubin Shahir's dates.

567
00:38:05,274 --> 00:38:07,786
I narrated our story to him,

568
00:38:07,913 --> 00:38:09,185
and he loved it too.

569
00:38:10,038 --> 00:38:11,771
Sir is flying back to Canada today.

570
00:38:11,772 --> 00:38:13,722
I may live in Canada,
but I'm a Kochi man at heart.

571
00:38:13,723 --> 00:38:16,844
So before I leave,
I thought I'd hand over the advance.

572
00:38:17,177 --> 00:38:18,793
Shall we?

573
00:38:19,012 --> 00:38:20,657
Face east.

574
00:38:20,658 --> 00:38:22,720
It's more auspicious.

575
00:38:24,063 --> 00:38:25,367
Here.

576
00:38:25,775 --> 00:38:26,957
- Shelly...
- Sir.

577
00:38:26,958 --> 00:38:28,838
Come here for a moment.

578
00:38:30,047 --> 00:38:31,370
All the best.

579
00:38:33,332 --> 00:38:34,415
I'll call you.

580
00:38:38,632 --> 00:38:41,221
What did you say happens
when someone touches that file?

581
00:38:43,066 --> 00:38:44,339
Count the zeroes.

582
00:38:44,340 --> 00:38:45,644
One lakh?!

583
00:38:48,274 --> 00:38:49,359
Hey...

584
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:50,401
Sir.

585
00:38:50,734 --> 00:38:53,134
Make a GD entry for this.
Mini still isn't here.

586
00:38:53,355 --> 00:38:54,504
Okay, sir.

587
00:39:50,474 --> 00:39:51,950
Sir, your tea.

588
00:40:41,906 --> 00:40:43,779
- Sir, can I get you another cup of tea?
- No.

589
00:40:47,044 --> 00:40:48,496
I'll take care of the rest, sir.

590
00:41:11,207 --> 00:41:12,843
Don't you have anything to study?

591
00:41:14,300 --> 00:41:15,307
Put that phone away.

592
00:41:15,399 --> 00:41:16,754
I'm teaching you today.

593
00:41:17,954 --> 00:41:19,364
Soumya, I bought some fruits.

594
00:41:20,086 --> 00:41:21,506
What's that?

595
00:41:21,951 --> 00:41:23,378
Gone, gone!

596
00:41:23,379 --> 00:41:24,845
- Be quiet!
- Not gone!

597
00:41:25,092 --> 00:41:26,312
- Give me that phone.
- Dad!

598
00:41:26,313 --> 00:41:27,320
Go study.

599
00:41:29,066 --> 00:41:30,073
Bring your books.

600
00:41:30,973 --> 00:41:32,366
What a mess you've made!

601
00:41:33,592 --> 00:41:35,898
Do you know how hard your mother works

602
00:41:36,306 --> 00:41:37,892
to keep this place clean?

603
00:41:38,473 --> 00:41:39,959
Go sit at the table.

604
00:41:47,565 --> 00:41:49,031
Sit and study. I'll be right back.

605
00:41:53,242 --> 00:41:54,650
<i>K for key.</i>

606
00:41:54,810 --> 00:41:56,104
<i>K for king.</i>

607
00:41:56,410 --> 00:41:57,937
<i>K for kite.</i>

608
00:41:57,938 --> 00:41:59,318
K for kitten.

609
00:41:59,522 --> 00:42:00,903
H for hat.

610
00:42:01,116 --> 00:42:02,636
- H for hen.
- Sit and study.

611
00:42:03,043 --> 00:42:04,483
H for house.

612
00:42:04,656 --> 00:42:06,058
H for heart.

613
00:42:06,832 --> 00:42:07,912
Soumya.

614
00:42:08,279 --> 00:42:09,705
Got any more clothes to wash?

615
00:42:11,043 --> 00:42:12,169
I for igloo.

616
00:42:12,356 --> 00:42:13,363
I for ink.

617
00:42:13,477 --> 00:42:14,502
J...

618
00:42:14,503 --> 00:42:16,374
T for table.

619
00:42:16,375 --> 00:42:17,770
T for tiger.

620
00:42:17,953 --> 00:42:19,275
T for tree.

621
00:42:19,883 --> 00:42:21,620
T for train. T for turtle.

622
00:42:21,621 --> 00:42:22,789
So dusty.

623
00:42:24,783 --> 00:42:27,375
Dad, I need to go potty.

624
00:42:28,337 --> 00:42:29,343
Go.

625
00:42:30,557 --> 00:42:32,155
Don't flush till I come see it.

626
00:42:46,909 --> 00:42:48,769
Our kids are such tricksters, aren't they?

627
00:42:49,289 --> 00:42:50,960
Not as bad as you.

628
00:42:52,863 --> 00:42:54,528
If you've got something to say, say it.

629
00:42:54,529 --> 00:42:55,656
Drop the act.

630
00:42:55,657 --> 00:42:57,235
Teaching the kids, cleaning up...

631
00:42:58,950 --> 00:43:00,143
Hey...

632
00:43:01,034 --> 00:43:02,892
The director liked one of my stories.

633
00:43:03,170 --> 00:43:04,470
He wants me to write it.

634
00:43:07,615 --> 00:43:09,342
Is this where you burn your trash?

635
00:43:09,343 --> 00:43:10,862
<i>Where else should we burn it?</i>

636
00:43:10,863 --> 00:43:12,803
If the smoke bothers you,
just shut the window.

637
00:43:15,880 --> 00:43:17,284
If you take leave for films again,

638
00:43:17,285 --> 00:43:18,505
I'm leaving with the kids.

639
00:43:24,737 --> 00:43:25,743
Argh!

640
00:43:25,892 --> 00:43:26,924
What's this, Soumya?

641
00:43:26,925 --> 00:43:28,438
You splashed dirty water all over me!

642
00:43:28,439 --> 00:43:29,632
Where else should I throw it?

643
00:43:29,633 --> 00:43:31,260
If it splashes on you, just step aside.

644
00:43:31,261 --> 00:43:32,803
<i>Soumya, don't be so cheap.</i>

645
00:43:32,804 --> 00:43:33,835
<i>I'm coming up there!</i>

646
00:43:33,836 --> 00:43:35,724
<i>Why are you just standing there?
Say something!</i>

647
00:43:35,725 --> 00:43:37,684
I'm sick of living in these quarters.

648
00:43:38,223 --> 00:43:40,922
Every time I try to get us out,
you hold me back.

649
00:43:41,802 --> 00:43:43,487
These struggles will never end.

650
00:43:45,323 --> 00:43:46,940
Our life is about to change.

651
00:43:47,857 --> 00:43:49,063
I wasn't lying.

652
00:43:51,317 --> 00:43:52,323
Look at this.

653
00:43:52,683 --> 00:43:54,039
My advance cheque.

654
00:44:06,649 --> 00:44:08,195
Now don't go spending it.

655
00:44:10,015 --> 00:44:11,650
If we have to repay this too,

656
00:44:11,651 --> 00:44:13,331
we've got nothing left to mortgage.

657
00:44:14,294 --> 00:44:15,450
I'll keep it.

658
00:44:29,337 --> 00:44:31,497
I called you so many times.
Why didn't you answer?

659
00:44:40,907 --> 00:44:42,380
What's the duty today?

660
00:44:42,636 --> 00:44:43,826
To the DPO.

661
00:44:43,827 --> 00:44:45,999
Need to collect some supplies
for the station store.

662
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:47,669
This could be useful to you too.

663
00:44:47,830 --> 00:44:49,277
How?

664
00:44:50,001 --> 00:44:52,641
Rajeev is there,
a guy I trained at the DCRB.

665
00:44:52,944 --> 00:44:55,671
He promised to get us a copy
of the 174 case file.

666
00:44:56,894 --> 00:44:58,407
- How's that?
- Seriously?

667
00:45:01,458 --> 00:45:02,718
If this works out,

668
00:45:03,073 --> 00:45:04,986
you'll land yourself
a killer role in my movie.

669
00:45:05,858 --> 00:45:07,218
- Promise?
- Yes.

670
00:45:08,779 --> 00:45:11,965
<i>We're dealing with the biggest land scam
Kerala has ever seen.</i>

671
00:45:12,658 --> 00:45:15,545
Similar cases have been reported
in several other districts as well.

672
00:45:16,248 --> 00:45:19,115
At present, six such cases
have been reported in Palakkad district.

673
00:45:19,823 --> 00:45:22,903
<i>A detailed investigation is underway.</i>

674
00:45:22,904 --> 00:45:24,662
<i>Where are the complainants from, sir?</i>

675
00:45:24,663 --> 00:45:28,735
<i>The first complaint came from farmers
in Chettur village.</i>

676
00:45:29,354 --> 00:45:31,767
<i>Since receiving the complaint
six months ago,</i>

677
00:45:31,768 --> 00:45:33,490
<i>a special police team has been...</i>

678
00:45:33,763 --> 00:45:35,347
Why isn't he answering his phone?

679
00:45:35,348 --> 00:45:37,266
What if he is unable to get us the file?

680
00:45:37,267 --> 00:45:38,779
Then he could've said so earlier.

681
00:45:39,819 --> 00:45:41,185
Should we go check on him?

682
00:45:42,289 --> 00:45:43,846
Open the door.

683
00:45:43,847 --> 00:45:45,421
Watch the head. Careful.

684
00:45:45,422 --> 00:45:46,615
That's Rajeev.

685
00:45:46,616 --> 00:45:48,032
Get in.

686
00:45:48,974 --> 00:45:50,131
Move in.

687
00:45:50,132 --> 00:45:51,405
- Let's move.
- Sir!

688
00:45:51,406 --> 00:45:52,456
What happened?

689
00:45:52,457 --> 00:45:54,510
He fell down the staircase.
He's got a head injury.

690
00:45:54,511 --> 00:45:56,155
Get going.

691
00:45:57,759 --> 00:45:58,877
Listen...

692
00:45:58,878 --> 00:46:00,373
You got the cheque, that's true.

693
00:46:00,540 --> 00:46:02,388
But I think the writer
was right after all.

694
00:46:03,078 --> 00:46:04,978
You're better off
staying away from this file.

695
00:46:15,507 --> 00:46:17,631
<i>In the film, 'Manichitrathazhu',</i>

696
00:46:17,632 --> 00:46:19,860
<i>where you were the second unit director,</i>

697
00:46:20,017 --> 00:46:22,284
<i>Sunny, played by Mohanlal,</i>

698
00:46:22,285 --> 00:46:25,874
<i>is portrayed as a
world-renowned psychiatrist,</i>

699
00:46:26,060 --> 00:46:28,629
<i>a leading expert in his field.</i>

700
00:46:28,958 --> 00:46:31,569
<i>But in the same film,</i>

701
00:46:31,570 --> 00:46:36,052
<i>Ganga's mental illness is treated and cured</i>

702
00:46:36,271 --> 00:46:41,643
<i>not through scientific methods,</i>

703
00:46:42,193 --> 00:46:45,490
but through black magic, pujas,

704
00:46:45,491 --> 00:46:49,892
chants and tantric rituals.

705
00:46:49,893 --> 00:46:52,975
Why did you choose that approach?

706
00:46:53,729 --> 00:46:57,196
If we'd used psychiatric techniques

707
00:46:57,499 --> 00:47:00,065
and portrayed mental health realistically,

708
00:47:00,066 --> 00:47:02,182
it would've been very difficult

709
00:47:02,183 --> 00:47:05,272
for the average audience to understand.

710
00:47:05,777 --> 00:47:09,817
<i>In their minds,
the spirit had to get justice.</i>

711
00:47:10,033 --> 00:47:14,084
<i>So our focus was on creating
a visual experience for the viewers.</i>

712
00:47:14,594 --> 00:47:15,626
<i>So, visually...</i>

713
00:47:15,627 --> 00:47:16,758
- Let's go?
- Yes.

714
00:47:16,759 --> 00:47:18,700
<i>The invocation of the spirit,</i>

715
00:47:19,028 --> 00:47:21,652
<i>the colourful, mystical setting,
the chants...</i>

716
00:47:21,653 --> 00:47:23,548
<i>It was about bringing the spirit out and...</i>

717
00:47:23,549 --> 00:47:25,913
Listen, Delta One's on night duty.

718
00:47:25,914 --> 00:47:28,089
Don't lose your job
watching that all night.

719
00:47:28,090 --> 00:47:29,097
No, sir.

720
00:47:29,646 --> 00:47:30,806
Here you go, sir.

721
00:47:49,352 --> 00:47:52,029
<i>Begin your night patrols.</i>

722
00:47:52,690 --> 00:47:54,847
<i>Carry out your duties diligently. Over.</i>

723
00:48:05,027 --> 00:48:06,625
<i>13... 13 Control.</i>

724
00:48:08,234 --> 00:48:09,955
<i>13... 13 Control... 13.</i>

725
00:48:11,623 --> 00:48:13,610
<i>Kongad PS Control.</i>

726
00:48:15,920 --> 00:48:17,420
<i>13... 13 Control.</i>

727
00:48:17,421 --> 00:48:18,665
13 answering. Over.

728
00:48:18,666 --> 00:48:20,091
<i>Kerala Legislative Assembly query.</i>

729
00:48:20,092 --> 00:48:22,773
<i>Send Sierra
details of every land fraud case</i>

730
00:48:23,111 --> 00:48:25,161
<i>reported under your station limits</i>

731
00:48:25,162 --> 00:48:26,831
<i>since this government came to power.</i>

732
00:48:27,091 --> 00:48:28,132
<i>Over.</i>

733
00:48:28,133 --> 00:48:29,252
Message received, sir.

734
00:48:29,253 --> 00:48:30,563
Will check and revert. Over.

735
00:48:33,890 --> 00:48:35,369
Sir, there's a KLA enquiry.

736
00:48:35,370 --> 00:48:36,951
They need the details right away.

737
00:48:37,250 --> 00:48:38,518
<i>That file is in the cupboard.</i>

738
00:48:38,883 --> 00:48:40,777
<i>The key is under my cushion.</i>

739
00:48:41,203 --> 00:48:42,210
Okay, sir.

740
00:48:44,226 --> 00:48:46,146
<i>Attention all night patrol units.</i>

741
00:48:46,566 --> 00:48:49,358
<i>Check all financial institutions,
places of worship and ATM kiosks.</i>

742
00:48:49,359 --> 00:48:51,032
<i>Also check all locked houses.</i>

743
00:48:51,771 --> 00:48:53,029
<i>Be thorough.</i>

744
00:48:53,344 --> 00:48:55,471
<i>Check all suspicious vehicles.</i>

745
00:48:56,129 --> 00:48:58,744
<i>Challenge any strangers.</i>

746
00:48:59,628 --> 00:49:02,475
<i>All officers must sign the Station Diary.</i>

747
00:49:02,859 --> 00:49:04,005
Over.

748
00:49:06,996 --> 00:49:08,409
Sierra 13 calling. Over.

749
00:49:08,593 --> 00:49:09,799
<i>Sierra answering.</i>

750
00:49:09,977 --> 00:49:12,603
Sir, regarding the KLA enquiry,
two cases were reported.

751
00:49:12,984 --> 00:49:14,158
<i>Roger. All clear.</i>

752
00:51:13,653 --> 00:51:15,247
<i>13 Mobile.
13 Mobile Control.</i>

753
00:51:15,409 --> 00:51:17,071
P13 Mobile One answering.

754
00:51:17,283 --> 00:51:20,275
<i>The loco pilot has reported
a run-over at Adichira.</i>

755
00:51:20,276 --> 00:51:24,382
<i>The location is railway marker 29/14. Over.</i>

756
00:51:25,070 --> 00:51:26,101
Message is clear, sir.

757
00:51:26,102 --> 00:51:27,108
Over.

758
00:51:29,063 --> 00:51:30,764
Sir, there's been a run-over.

759
00:51:47,866 --> 00:51:48,873
What happened, sir?

760
00:51:51,619 --> 00:51:52,772
Tonight's <i>Panchami</i>.

761
00:51:56,090 --> 00:51:58,907
They say if someone dies on <i>Panchami</i>,
five more deaths will follow.

762
00:52:00,001 --> 00:52:02,027
How many more untimely deaths
will we have to see?

763
00:52:02,868 --> 00:52:04,594
And there have been all these bad omens.

764
00:52:09,121 --> 00:52:10,487
Sir, this is marker 29/14.

765
00:52:53,669 --> 00:52:55,448
Control P13 Mobile One calling.

766
00:52:55,584 --> 00:52:56,654
<i>Control answering.</i>

767
00:52:56,655 --> 00:52:58,907
Sir, the girl found on the railway track
is still alive.

768
00:52:58,908 --> 00:52:59,947
She's bleeding badly.

769
00:52:59,948 --> 00:53:01,878
We're taking her to the hospital. Over.

770
00:53:01,879 --> 00:53:02,988
<i>Message is clear. Over.</i>

771
00:53:02,989 --> 00:53:04,167
Come on, hurry!

772
00:53:04,168 --> 00:53:05,174
Okay, sir.

773
00:53:15,394 --> 00:53:16,628
Take that bag.

774
00:53:21,263 --> 00:53:22,331
Did you check for a phone?

775
00:53:22,530 --> 00:53:23,967
Sir, I only found this card.

776
00:53:23,968 --> 00:53:25,093
It has a phone number.

777
00:53:28,909 --> 00:53:29,973
Sir, what happened?

778
00:53:29,974 --> 00:53:31,041
She was hit by a train.

779
00:53:33,837 --> 00:53:35,456
We need to stabilise her first

780
00:53:35,457 --> 00:53:37,047
and shift her for a CT scan.

781
00:53:37,916 --> 00:53:39,079
Sir, any relatives?

782
00:53:39,317 --> 00:53:40,824
We haven't identified her yet.

783
00:53:41,128 --> 00:53:43,074
Sister, start Lorazepam 4 mg IV.

784
00:54:04,892 --> 00:54:05,906
Hello?

785
00:54:06,419 --> 00:54:08,419
Is this Karthika's house?

786
00:54:08,816 --> 00:54:10,269
<i>Yes, this is Karthika speaking.</i>

787
00:54:12,027 --> 00:54:13,060
<i>Hello?</i>

788
00:54:14,075 --> 00:54:15,121
<i>Hello?</i>

789
00:54:40,263 --> 00:54:41,693
Sir, why is there no power?

790
00:54:41,694 --> 00:54:43,091
Lightning took the power out, sir.

791
00:54:43,092 --> 00:54:44,599
Sir, he's the Ponnani IP.

792
00:54:45,296 --> 00:54:46,469
- Sir.
- Where's GD?

793
00:54:46,470 --> 00:54:48,313
He's out on night patrol, sir.
Staff shortage.

794
00:54:48,314 --> 00:54:50,003
We brought someone in for questioning.
Bring him.

795
00:54:50,004 --> 00:54:51,256
Why are you pulling away?

796
00:54:51,347 --> 00:54:52,481
Go on!

797
00:54:53,128 --> 00:54:54,841
- Walk!
- Stand over there.

798
00:54:55,727 --> 00:54:57,518
Sir! I don't know anything.

799
00:54:57,519 --> 00:54:58,912
I know you know.

800
00:54:59,030 --> 00:55:00,660
- Sir, I don't know.
- You'll talk.

801
00:55:03,746 --> 00:55:05,820
Tell us where he is.
Save yourself the trouble.

802
00:55:06,590 --> 00:55:08,068
This is a POCSO case.

803
00:55:08,069 --> 00:55:09,695
You won't be seeing daylight again.

804
00:55:09,696 --> 00:55:11,004
I told you... I don't know, sir.

805
00:55:12,026 --> 00:55:14,233
Let's see how long you hold out.

806
00:55:29,176 --> 00:55:30,200
Hey, you.

807
00:55:30,822 --> 00:55:32,747
Bring him here.
I'll make him talk.

808
00:55:33,739 --> 00:55:35,164
- What, huh?
- I don't know, sir.

809
00:55:35,165 --> 00:55:36,251
Come on...

810
00:55:39,805 --> 00:55:42,045
She's just a schoolgirl and you...

811
00:55:45,347 --> 00:55:47,393
His last call was to your number.

812
00:55:48,441 --> 00:55:49,545
Both his phone and hers

813
00:55:49,546 --> 00:55:51,701
last switched off
on the same tower location.

814
00:55:52,499 --> 00:55:53,939
You better tell the truth.

815
00:56:00,093 --> 00:56:01,679
- Drop the act.
- I don't know, sir.

816
00:56:03,384 --> 00:56:04,384
Sir...

817
00:56:06,769 --> 00:56:08,293
- Come on, say it.
- I will tell, sir...

818
00:56:08,294 --> 00:56:09,450
I'll tell you, sir...

819
00:56:09,451 --> 00:56:10,520
I'll tell you...

820
00:56:12,249 --> 00:56:13,411
They're in Nenmara...

821
00:56:13,585 --> 00:56:14,772
At Star Lodge...

822
00:56:24,800 --> 00:56:25,857
Keep an eye on him.

823
00:56:25,858 --> 00:56:26,960
We'll go get the other one.

824
00:56:50,579 --> 00:56:51,586
Sir...

825
00:56:52,146 --> 00:56:53,318
I need to use the toilet.

826
00:57:02,226 --> 00:57:04,180
Do you want to go to the hospital?

827
00:57:10,700 --> 00:57:11,706
Get up.

828
00:59:14,350 --> 00:59:15,435
Hello.

829
00:59:15,599 --> 00:59:17,420
<i>Can you take a day off today?</i>

830
00:59:17,421 --> 00:59:19,304
<i>I need to talk to you about something.</i>

831
00:59:19,548 --> 00:59:21,774
No, I can't take the day off today.
A truck is coming.

832
00:59:21,775 --> 00:59:23,507
I have to load and dispatch 2,000 boxes.

833
00:59:24,259 --> 00:59:25,493
What is it about?

834
00:59:25,494 --> 00:59:26,556
<i>Well...</i>

835
00:59:26,557 --> 00:59:29,485
<i>I really need to see you.</i>

836
00:59:51,286 --> 00:59:53,259
Stop stomping around and open that door!

837
00:59:56,209 --> 00:59:58,076
Are you sleeping
with the station locked up?

838
00:59:58,077 --> 00:59:59,742
Sir, I had just gone to the toilet.

839
01:00:00,420 --> 01:00:01,749
What's this blood?

840
01:00:02,805 --> 01:00:05,733
Sir, it got stained when I took the man
in the cell to the bathroom.

841
01:00:05,734 --> 01:00:07,092
Give that to me.

842
01:00:08,290 --> 01:00:09,514
What's the case?

843
01:00:09,515 --> 01:00:10,875
Has he been medically examined?

844
01:00:10,876 --> 01:00:13,547
Sir, a squad from Ponnani brought him here.

845
01:00:13,883 --> 01:00:15,501
Did you enter it in the sentry register?

846
01:00:18,646 --> 01:00:21,290
Did anyone inform
the SHO or GD that he's here?

847
01:00:23,068 --> 01:00:24,851
Did you inform them?

848
01:00:25,345 --> 01:00:26,431
No, sir.

849
01:00:27,080 --> 01:00:29,151
Are you a fool,
or are you pretending to be one?

850
01:00:30,290 --> 01:00:32,353
Do you know
how many people could lose their jobs

851
01:00:32,354 --> 01:00:33,650
if something happens to him?

852
01:00:34,004 --> 01:00:35,158
Bloody useless!

853
01:00:35,159 --> 01:00:36,650
You're not fit for this job.

854
01:00:42,291 --> 01:00:44,263
You have no sense of responsibility,
right, Shelley?

855
01:00:44,264 --> 01:00:46,588
How long have I been working like a dog?

856
01:00:48,935 --> 01:00:50,478
You and your damn cinema!

857
01:00:53,319 --> 01:00:55,072
The only reason I'm still chasing cinema

858
01:00:55,073 --> 01:00:57,728
is to somehow get you and the kids out
from this hell.

859
01:00:59,803 --> 01:01:01,709
I don't have any other way out.

860
01:01:04,244 --> 01:01:07,170
I went back to this job only for you.

861
01:01:08,564 --> 01:01:10,795
I didn't get suspended on purpose.

862
01:01:17,866 --> 01:01:19,906
What if something had happened to that boy?

863
01:01:20,071 --> 01:01:21,536
What would've become of us?

864
01:01:21,726 --> 01:01:23,470
If it were up to me,
I'd have dismissed you.

865
01:01:25,624 --> 01:01:28,028
The producer has rented a flat in Kochi.

866
01:01:29,745 --> 01:01:31,215
He wants me to stay there.

867
01:01:54,910 --> 01:01:56,762
Can't you write from the quarters?

868
01:01:56,913 --> 01:01:58,100
Isn't that enough?

869
01:02:16,263 --> 01:02:19,287
<i>Come out already. I'm getting late.</i>

870
01:02:25,192 --> 01:02:26,347
There you are.

871
01:02:26,554 --> 01:02:28,692
I've kept food for you
and for the kids this evening.

872
01:02:28,693 --> 01:02:30,675
Pick both of them up
when the school bus arrives.

873
01:02:30,676 --> 01:02:33,080
And give them food
before sending them to tuition.

874
01:02:33,176 --> 01:02:34,864
Don't forget while you're busy
smoking and daydreaming.

875
01:02:34,865 --> 01:02:36,121
- Don't you need the key?
- Oh no!

876
01:02:44,767 --> 01:02:47,173
Soumya, I moved your scooter
because I'm washing the car.

877
01:02:49,286 --> 01:02:51,519
Shelley sir is under suspension, right?

878
01:02:53,713 --> 01:02:54,832
Well, unlike Sumesh sir,

879
01:02:54,833 --> 01:02:56,756
his job isn't carrying
the SP's briefcase around.

880
01:02:57,257 --> 01:02:58,597
He works in a local station.

881
01:02:58,777 --> 01:03:00,628
Besides, aren't you the ones who always say

882
01:03:00,629 --> 01:03:02,934
suspension is part
of a policeman's life, sir?

883
01:03:04,896 --> 01:03:06,839
That was so unnecessary!

884
01:03:22,827 --> 01:03:23,891
Hello.

885
01:03:23,892 --> 01:03:25,754
<i>Hey, I found the address
of Narayanan Sharma,</i>

886
01:03:25,755 --> 01:03:27,231
<i>who investigated the 174 case.</i>

887
01:03:27,232 --> 01:03:28,347
That's great.

888
01:03:28,348 --> 01:03:30,000
<i>I've been digging through old newspapers.</i>

889
01:03:30,001 --> 01:03:32,492
- Didn't find a thing.
- <i>I'll WhatsApp you the address.</i>

890
01:03:32,493 --> 01:03:33,977
- <i>Take a look.</i>
- Okay.

891
01:04:09,451 --> 01:04:10,874
Name and birth star?

892
01:04:11,918 --> 01:04:13,850
Shelley.
I'm a policeman.

893
01:04:14,930 --> 01:04:15,992
Birth star?

894
01:04:15,993 --> 01:04:18,090
Sir, I didn't come here
for an astrology reading.

895
01:04:18,091 --> 01:04:20,641
Back when you were at Kongad Station,
didn't you investigate

896
01:04:20,642 --> 01:04:22,828
the case of a woman found dead
on the railway tracks?

897
01:04:23,666 --> 01:04:25,554
I came to learn more about that case.

898
01:04:30,243 --> 01:04:33,069
That station is still
plagued by trouble, isn't it?

899
01:04:33,718 --> 01:04:34,765
Yes, sir.

900
01:04:35,186 --> 01:04:37,826
The soul of the deceased
hasn't found peace.

901
01:04:39,316 --> 01:04:41,596
The death happened
under the <i>Pooruruttathi</i> star.

902
01:04:42,251 --> 01:04:43,702
And on a <i>Panchami</i> day.

903
01:04:43,948 --> 01:04:46,953
Ordinary funeral rites
won't be enough.

904
01:04:47,086 --> 01:04:49,070
Special rituals are required.

905
01:04:50,653 --> 01:04:51,653
See, it's true.

906
01:04:52,952 --> 01:04:54,616
Do you believe all this?

907
01:04:58,296 --> 01:05:00,736
Sir, what made you so sure
it was murder?

908
01:05:05,240 --> 01:05:07,132
<i>Listen, I was the one
who carried that girl.</i>

909
01:05:07,899 --> 01:05:10,078
<i>The only injury she had
was a wound on her head,</i>

910
01:05:10,079 --> 01:05:12,377
<i>as though someone had struck her
with an iron rod.</i>

911
01:05:12,510 --> 01:05:14,275
<i>If she had jumped from a moving train,</i>

912
01:05:14,276 --> 01:05:16,431
<i>shouldn't her body be covered in abrasions?</i>

913
01:05:16,557 --> 01:05:18,066
There were no other injuries.

914
01:05:18,377 --> 01:05:20,811
Someone deliberately struck her
on the head with an iron rod

915
01:05:20,812 --> 01:05:22,479
and dumped her on the tracks.

916
01:05:22,480 --> 01:05:24,788
She must've still had
a faint bit of consciousness left,

917
01:05:24,789 --> 01:05:27,053
so she rolled aside
before the train hit her.

918
01:05:33,303 --> 01:05:35,514
Sir, you once said the deceased herself

919
01:05:35,515 --> 01:05:37,466
answered your call that day.

920
01:05:56,176 --> 01:05:58,710
Hey, my dad is calling you inside.

921
01:06:07,092 --> 01:06:08,968
The girls were twins.

922
01:06:09,260 --> 01:06:10,890
Karthika and Keerthana.

923
01:06:11,330 --> 01:06:13,213
They worked at the same place.

924
01:06:14,836 --> 01:06:16,340
It was Keerthana who died.

925
01:06:16,880 --> 01:06:19,321
That day, she'd accidentally taken
her sister's ID card.

926
01:06:19,885 --> 01:06:21,900
That's why
I ended up calling Karthika.

927
01:06:27,195 --> 01:06:29,401
Since the deceased girl's phone
was missing,

928
01:06:29,738 --> 01:06:31,261
I pulled its cell tower records.

929
01:06:31,694 --> 01:06:33,601
Comparing them
with her previous locations,

930
01:06:33,794 --> 01:06:35,657
I found she usually boarded trains

931
01:06:35,658 --> 01:06:37,430
from a station near Coimbatore.

932
01:06:38,365 --> 01:06:40,040
But that day,
she never boarded a train.

933
01:06:40,391 --> 01:06:41,446
Instead,

934
01:06:41,821 --> 01:06:46,391
she boarded a bus somewhere
between Coimbatore and Walayar.

935
01:06:48,495 --> 01:06:50,344
Her phone was switched off

936
01:06:50,345 --> 01:06:52,048
at the Palakkad bus stand.

937
01:06:54,186 --> 01:06:56,671
When I checked the CCTV footage
from the bus stand,

938
01:06:56,888 --> 01:06:58,414
I became suspicious

939
01:06:58,781 --> 01:07:02,734
and began investigating
what happened there that night.

940
01:07:04,880 --> 01:07:07,889
Yes, sir. I took that girl
from here to the station.

941
01:07:07,890 --> 01:07:08,981
What happened, sir?

942
01:07:08,982 --> 01:07:11,411
Didn't you hear she was found dead
on the railway tracks?

943
01:07:11,412 --> 01:07:12,498
No, sir.

944
01:07:12,499 --> 01:07:14,757
Wasn't it you
who dumped her on the tracks?

945
01:07:15,885 --> 01:07:17,295
No, sir. I didn't.

946
01:07:17,296 --> 01:07:19,552
The last place her phone was switched off
was right here.

947
01:07:20,077 --> 01:07:21,498
And the phone is missing.

948
01:07:21,594 --> 01:07:22,655
Tell me the truth.

949
01:07:23,375 --> 01:07:25,216
You were the last person seen with her.

950
01:07:27,290 --> 01:07:30,496
Sir, there's a wretched woman
named Swapna.

951
01:07:30,497 --> 01:07:33,019
I saw her bump into that girl yesterday.

952
01:07:33,168 --> 01:07:35,088
She must be the one who stole the phone.

953
01:07:35,213 --> 01:07:36,517
Where can I find her?

954
01:07:36,518 --> 01:07:37,961
I don't know where she lives, sir.

955
01:07:38,236 --> 01:07:40,811
But she'll be there by 8:00 or 8:30 p.m.

956
01:08:10,838 --> 01:08:12,525
- Get in.
- How many of you are in the car?!

957
01:08:13,120 --> 01:08:14,519
- Sit still.
- Let go of my hand!

958
01:08:14,520 --> 01:08:16,384
- Hey! Let go!
- Don't move. Sit still!

959
01:08:17,502 --> 01:08:18,964
Let go of my hand!
Let go of me!

960
01:08:18,965 --> 01:08:20,292
Didn't I tell you to not move?

961
01:08:20,409 --> 01:08:21,666
Stop the vehicle!

962
01:08:25,149 --> 01:08:27,229
Sir, it was an accidental death.

963
01:08:27,230 --> 01:08:28,423
No doubt about it.

964
01:08:28,624 --> 01:08:31,502
The forensic and post-mortem reports
confirm it.

965
01:08:31,694 --> 01:08:33,556
Close the case immediately.

966
01:08:33,557 --> 01:08:34,643
Sir...

967
01:08:36,940 --> 01:08:38,447
- Let go of me!
- Don't make a sound.

968
01:08:38,448 --> 01:08:40,621
- Let go of my hand. I'll get down myself.
- Don't create a scene in here.

969
01:08:40,622 --> 01:08:41,940
Let go of my hand, you!

970
01:08:42,050 --> 01:08:43,375
What's going on here?

971
01:08:43,376 --> 01:08:44,783
Sir, last night I suspected

972
01:08:44,784 --> 01:08:46,650
the girl's death
might've been a murder.

973
01:08:46,807 --> 01:08:48,376
So I brought her in for questioning.

974
01:08:48,377 --> 01:08:49,915
Who told you it was murder?

975
01:08:50,163 --> 01:08:52,440
Did I assign you that case?

976
01:08:52,441 --> 01:08:53,589
No, right?

977
01:08:55,124 --> 01:08:57,447
After reading a few detective novels,

978
01:08:57,448 --> 01:08:59,432
you think you're Sherlock Holmes?

979
01:09:00,304 --> 01:09:01,649
Even if it was murder,

980
01:09:01,764 --> 01:09:04,947
you can't bring a woman to the station
at night without a woman officer.

981
01:09:06,550 --> 01:09:07,854
The government doesn't pay you

982
01:09:07,855 --> 01:09:09,939
to solve cases with horoscopes
and fortune-telling.

983
01:09:10,832 --> 01:09:12,293
Send her away immediately.

984
01:09:12,294 --> 01:09:13,957
Or you'll lose your job.

985
01:09:23,571 --> 01:09:25,476
So you never investigated after that?

986
01:09:25,477 --> 01:09:27,401
Then the woman filed a complaint.

987
01:09:27,402 --> 01:09:29,151
All four of us were suspended.

988
01:09:29,255 --> 01:09:31,458
By the time I was reinstated,
I'd already retired.

989
01:09:32,259 --> 01:09:33,845
Who investigated it then?

990
01:09:34,866 --> 01:09:37,346
CI Sathyajith closed the case.

991
01:09:39,066 --> 01:09:41,816
Sir, I'm writing
a story based on this file.

992
01:09:42,234 --> 01:09:44,994
If I could get your case diary,
it'd really help.

993
01:09:54,736 --> 01:09:56,675
What's your birth star and age?

994
01:09:57,248 --> 01:09:58,253
Vishakham.

995
01:09:58,466 --> 01:09:59,808
I'm forty-one.

996
01:10:00,226 --> 01:10:01,625
You're going through a bad phase.

997
01:10:01,626 --> 01:10:03,714
Be careful pursuing this.

998
01:10:32,655 --> 01:10:33,837
Hello.

999
01:10:36,924 --> 01:10:39,053
When?! Where?!

1000
01:10:50,254 --> 01:10:52,382
- No, no, no! It's over!
- I've got you!

1001
01:10:52,383 --> 01:10:55,047
- It's over.
- It's over. It's over.

1002
01:10:55,281 --> 01:10:57,507
It's over. You're alright.

1003
01:11:06,104 --> 01:11:08,189
Where the hell have you been all this time?

1004
01:11:09,066 --> 01:11:10,209
I...

1005
01:11:10,210 --> 01:11:12,784
went to meet someone about the story.

1006
01:11:13,634 --> 01:11:15,577
You and your damn movie!

1007
01:11:16,294 --> 01:11:17,973
Didn't I tell you a hundred times

1008
01:11:17,974 --> 01:11:19,843
to bring the kids home on time?

1009
01:11:19,844 --> 01:11:21,204
Didn't I?!

1010
01:11:21,205 --> 01:11:22,486
Hey, lower your voice.

1011
01:11:22,806 --> 01:11:24,686
If anything had happened to my child...

1012
01:11:25,454 --> 01:11:26,757
People are listening!

1013
01:11:26,758 --> 01:11:28,016
Let everyone hear!

1014
01:11:28,695 --> 01:11:29,958
Instead of going to work,

1015
01:11:29,959 --> 01:11:32,132
- he runs around chasing cinema like a clown
- Dear...

1016
01:11:32,133 --> 01:11:34,516
- I've kept this bottled up for years.
- Dear...

1017
01:11:34,930 --> 01:11:36,859
Do you know how much debt
he's piled up?

1018
01:11:36,994 --> 01:11:38,742
Dear... enough.

1019
01:11:38,743 --> 01:11:41,338
Aren't you the ones
who saddled me with him?

1020
01:11:41,426 --> 01:11:43,843
Hey, this is a hospital.
Don't create a scene.

1021
01:11:45,243 --> 01:11:46,438
Sir...

1022
01:11:48,338 --> 01:11:49,474
Dad...

1023
01:11:49,926 --> 01:11:52,336
I was watching her.

1024
01:11:52,337 --> 01:11:55,259
But she slipped away and ran off.

1025
01:11:57,647 --> 01:11:58,736
It's okay.

1026
01:12:02,180 --> 01:12:04,031
Go sit with Mom.

1027
01:12:04,032 --> 01:12:05,523
I'll be outside.

1028
01:12:05,625 --> 01:12:06,719
Go on.

1029
01:12:12,059 --> 01:12:14,633
Don't take what she said personally.
Let it go.

1030
01:12:14,634 --> 01:12:16,380
How's the pain?

1031
01:12:16,381 --> 01:12:17,834
You'll be fine soon.

1032
01:12:21,711 --> 01:12:22,896
Dad...

1033
01:12:22,897 --> 01:12:24,514
Soumya, I've brought the car.

1034
01:12:28,906 --> 01:12:30,115
Soumya...

1035
01:12:31,475 --> 01:12:32,600
Please.

1036
01:12:33,306 --> 01:12:35,004
I'm falling apart.

1037
01:12:35,103 --> 01:12:36,591
I just want some peace of mind.

1038
01:12:36,592 --> 01:12:38,048
Please don't make this harder for me.

1039
01:12:54,556 --> 01:12:57,311
Seeing the hanging body's feet
touching the floor,

1040
01:12:57,927 --> 01:12:59,123
a police officer,

1041
01:12:59,213 --> 01:13:01,577
said aloud in front of the locals
that it was murder.

1042
01:13:02,627 --> 01:13:05,308
Even after it was scientifically proven
to be suicide...

1043
01:13:05,599 --> 01:13:08,532
people still believe it was murder.

1044
01:13:08,712 --> 01:13:10,524
And that the police buried the case.

1045
01:13:11,580 --> 01:13:13,206
What I want to tell you is this.

1046
01:13:13,593 --> 01:13:14,959
When you're at a crime scene

1047
01:13:14,960 --> 01:13:16,120
during an investigation,

1048
01:13:16,365 --> 01:13:18,673
don't say careless things
in front of the public.

1049
01:13:20,394 --> 01:13:21,400
Class over.

1050
01:13:21,666 --> 01:13:22,906
Class rise.

1051
01:13:23,339 --> 01:13:24,572
Attention.

1052
01:13:28,227 --> 01:13:29,234
Sir, I'm Shelly.

1053
01:13:30,426 --> 01:13:31,846
Your producer had called me.

1054
01:13:32,167 --> 01:13:34,493
It's about the 174 case
from Kongad station, right?

1055
01:13:34,494 --> 01:13:35,394
Yes, sir.

1056
01:13:35,395 --> 01:13:37,383
You could just pull the file and check.

1057
01:13:37,940 --> 01:13:39,780
Sir, no one dares touch that file.

1058
01:13:41,574 --> 01:13:43,579
They believe that if you touch it

1059
01:13:43,580 --> 01:13:46,135
the girl's spirit gets officers suspended,

1060
01:13:46,560 --> 01:13:48,002
stains their uniforms with blood

1061
01:13:48,173 --> 01:13:50,600
and brings more unnatural deaths.

1062
01:13:52,140 --> 01:13:53,466
Tell me...

1063
01:13:53,467 --> 01:13:55,219
which station is free of unnatural deaths,

1064
01:13:55,220 --> 01:13:56,227
suspensions,

1065
01:13:56,407 --> 01:13:58,867
or blood on uniforms?

1066
01:14:00,153 --> 01:14:02,387
If that were true,
I should've been the first to suffer.

1067
01:14:02,500 --> 01:14:04,133
I investigated and closed that case.

1068
01:14:05,807 --> 01:14:06,814
Sir, I've a doubt.

1069
01:14:08,747 --> 01:14:10,536
If she fell from a moving train,

1070
01:14:10,807 --> 01:14:11,953
shouldn't there be

1071
01:14:11,954 --> 01:14:13,455
more injuries on her body?

1072
01:14:14,074 --> 01:14:15,104
But in this case,

1073
01:14:15,105 --> 01:14:16,519
there was only one wound,

1074
01:14:16,520 --> 01:14:17,953
as if struck by an iron rod.

1075
01:14:21,213 --> 01:14:22,561
<i>The dead girl's house</i>

1076
01:14:22,562 --> 01:14:25,456
<i>was just a hundred metres from the scene.</i>

1077
01:14:25,679 --> 01:14:27,704
<i>The train had stopped there
waiting for the signal</i>

1078
01:14:27,705 --> 01:14:29,087
<i>when she tried to get off.</i>

1079
01:14:29,907 --> 01:14:31,925
<i>Just as she reached the door,</i>

1080
01:14:31,926 --> 01:14:33,479
<i>the train suddenly started moving...</i>

1081
01:14:33,480 --> 01:14:36,455
<i>the door hit her and she fell.</i>

1082
01:14:42,492 --> 01:14:43,794
She died after hitting her head

1083
01:14:43,795 --> 01:14:45,323
on the concrete block near the track.

1084
01:14:45,820 --> 01:14:48,071
The forensic evidence supported that.

1085
01:14:49,287 --> 01:14:51,342
Sir, I met Narayana Sharma,

1086
01:14:51,343 --> 01:14:52,925
the officer who first handled the case.

1087
01:14:53,400 --> 01:14:55,166
He said she had a fight

1088
01:14:55,167 --> 01:14:57,315
with a woman at the bus stand.

1089
01:14:57,840 --> 01:15:00,579
He says it may be connected to her death.

1090
01:15:00,580 --> 01:15:02,540
That woman was a local prostitute.

1091
01:15:02,920 --> 01:15:04,559
When they bumped into each other...

1092
01:15:04,560 --> 01:15:06,341
the girl's phone ended up with her.

1093
01:15:06,653 --> 01:15:08,948
She handed it over immediately
to a policeman there.

1094
01:15:10,554 --> 01:15:14,286
Sir, she usually takes the train
from Coimbatore after work.

1095
01:15:15,200 --> 01:15:16,365
But that day,

1096
01:15:16,366 --> 01:15:19,007
she came by bus to Palakkad stand.

1097
01:15:19,540 --> 01:15:20,986
Doesn't that seem unusual?

1098
01:15:20,987 --> 01:15:22,580
She went shopping after work,

1099
01:15:22,678 --> 01:15:24,918
got late and missed the train.

1100
01:15:25,260 --> 01:15:26,267
So she took a bus.

1101
01:15:26,520 --> 01:15:27,874
What's unusual about that?

1102
01:15:29,400 --> 01:15:31,233
The first questions you ask in a case are

1103
01:15:31,234 --> 01:15:34,115
who, when, where, how and why.

1104
01:15:34,940 --> 01:15:37,200
None of those raised
any suspicion in this case.

1105
01:15:38,667 --> 01:15:40,777
It was that astrologer
and his nonsense about spirits

1106
01:15:40,778 --> 01:15:42,343
that turned it into a mess.

1107
01:15:58,540 --> 01:16:00,358
<i>The first questions you ask in a case are</i>

1108
01:16:00,359 --> 01:16:03,185
<i>who, when, where, how and why.</i>

1109
01:16:05,275 --> 01:16:07,044
<i>If she jumped off a train,</i>

1110
01:16:07,228 --> 01:16:09,285
<i>shouldn't her body be covered in abrasions?</i>

1111
01:16:09,286 --> 01:16:11,233
<i>But there were no other injuries.</i>

1112
01:16:11,234 --> 01:16:13,660
<i>Someone deliberately struck her
on the head with an iron rod</i>

1113
01:16:13,661 --> 01:16:15,441
<i>and dumped her on the tracks.</i>

1114
01:16:18,815 --> 01:16:20,112
<i>She died after hitting her head</i>

1115
01:16:20,113 --> 01:16:21,987
<i>on the concrete block near the track.</i>

1116
01:16:22,155 --> 01:16:24,415
<i>The forensic evidence supported that.</i>

1117
01:17:07,687 --> 01:17:08,694
Want one?

1118
01:17:10,460 --> 01:17:11,467
No.

1119
01:17:19,480 --> 01:17:21,579
Those of us in the film industry...

1120
01:17:21,580 --> 01:17:24,226
our lives aren't what people think.

1121
01:17:26,840 --> 01:17:28,161
The funny thing is,

1122
01:17:29,107 --> 01:17:31,230
you'd think at least
your family would understand.

1123
01:17:32,140 --> 01:17:33,147
But no.

1124
01:17:36,187 --> 01:17:38,617
Whatever people think of those in films...

1125
01:17:38,618 --> 01:17:40,350
our families think the same.

1126
01:17:41,587 --> 01:17:44,100
Once you get into cinema,

1127
01:17:44,560 --> 01:17:46,526
don't expect peace at home.

1128
01:17:52,027 --> 01:17:53,180
All we can do

1129
01:17:54,267 --> 01:17:55,658
is support them financially

1130
01:17:55,659 --> 01:17:57,404
whenever we can.

1131
01:17:58,266 --> 01:17:59,512
That's about all we can do.

1132
01:18:05,340 --> 01:18:07,532
If you carry all this inside...

1133
01:18:08,933 --> 01:18:10,729
you'll never make a film.

1134
01:18:16,733 --> 01:18:18,120
It's already been three weeks.

1135
01:18:20,014 --> 01:18:21,727
Don't take this the wrong way.

1136
01:18:22,934 --> 01:18:25,447
The producer's putting money into this
because he trusts me.

1137
01:18:27,360 --> 01:18:28,367
Sir...

1138
01:18:28,767 --> 01:18:30,106
That's not the reason...

1139
01:18:32,114 --> 01:18:34,434
I'm just confused
about one part of the story.

1140
01:18:35,660 --> 01:18:38,620
Then why don't we bring in
someone experienced to write with you?

1141
01:18:42,496 --> 01:18:44,542
Sir, please give me a little more time.

1142
01:18:45,894 --> 01:18:47,512
Let me try once more.

1143
01:18:55,480 --> 01:18:56,657
Three days max.

1144
01:18:57,487 --> 01:18:59,383
After that, I don't want any excuses.

1145
01:19:00,433 --> 01:19:01,728
Or I'm out.

1146
01:19:22,576 --> 01:19:25,436
<i>She died after hitting her head
on the concrete block near the track.</i>

1147
01:19:25,867 --> 01:19:28,093
<i>The forensic evidence supported that.</i>

1148
01:19:28,811 --> 01:19:30,271
<i>Three days max.</i>

1149
01:19:30,506 --> 01:19:32,638
<i>After that, I don't want any excuses.</i>

1150
01:22:08,607 --> 01:22:10,781
<i>Dad, look, my wounds have healed.</i>

1151
01:22:11,862 --> 01:22:13,175
<i>Dad, where are you?</i>

1152
01:22:13,493 --> 01:22:14,642
I...

1153
01:22:15,546 --> 01:22:16,739
...am in Ernakulam.

1154
01:22:17,605 --> 01:22:19,126
<i>Dad, is your work over?</i>

1155
01:22:19,127 --> 01:22:20,455
<i>Is your work over, Dad?</i>

1156
01:22:20,456 --> 01:22:21,613
<i>Give me the phone!</i>

1157
01:22:21,614 --> 01:22:23,246
<i>- Let me talk.
- I will ask.</i>

1158
01:22:23,247 --> 01:22:24,540
<i>Let go of the phone.</i>

1159
01:22:24,827 --> 01:22:27,007
- Where's Mom?
- She's here.

1160
01:22:30,173 --> 01:22:31,179
Soumya...

1161
01:22:34,733 --> 01:22:35,740
Soumya...

1162
01:22:37,315 --> 01:22:39,120
I can't live without you all.

1163
01:22:41,895 --> 01:22:43,081
Can I come back?

1164
01:22:45,760 --> 01:22:46,767
Come home.

1165
01:23:21,183 --> 01:23:22,190
What happened?

1166
01:23:23,344 --> 01:23:24,856
You didn't even finish your dinner.

1167
01:23:36,164 --> 01:23:37,893
You can deposit that cheque.

1168
01:23:38,684 --> 01:23:40,045
Did you finish the story?

1169
01:23:41,223 --> 01:23:42,230
No.

1170
01:23:46,723 --> 01:23:48,601
I don't think I can do it...

1171
01:23:53,235 --> 01:23:54,906
The director is very worried.

1172
01:23:57,957 --> 01:23:59,783
They're bringing in another writer...

1173
01:24:01,190 --> 01:24:02,197
to finish it.

1174
01:24:06,432 --> 01:24:07,988
I'll still get story credit.

1175
01:24:13,363 --> 01:24:14,670
It's okay.

1176
01:24:15,689 --> 01:24:17,351
At least you got your break in films.

1177
01:24:19,424 --> 01:24:21,077
So many people don't get even that.

1178
01:24:22,087 --> 01:24:23,658
I need to get back on duty soon.

1179
01:24:25,368 --> 01:24:26,575
I'll speak to Sumesh sir...

1180
01:24:27,066 --> 01:24:28,376
and meet the SP.

1181
01:24:37,000 --> 01:24:38,007
You were right.

1182
01:24:42,487 --> 01:24:44,468
Maybe I'm just not good enough.

1183
01:25:29,618 --> 01:25:31,345
<i>P13... P13 Control.</i>

1184
01:25:33,476 --> 01:25:35,423
<i>Kongad PS... Kongad PS Control.</i>

1185
01:25:36,103 --> 01:25:37,260
Answering. Over.

1186
01:25:40,824 --> 01:25:42,243
Kongad PS answering. Over.

1187
01:25:45,694 --> 01:25:46,940
<i>P13 Control.</i>

1188
01:25:51,472 --> 01:25:52,905
<i>Control P13 Mobile calling.</i>

1189
01:25:53,842 --> 01:25:54,951
<i>Control answering.</i>

1190
01:25:54,952 --> 01:25:56,977
<i>The girl found on the railway track
is still alive.</i>

1191
01:25:56,978 --> 01:25:58,071
<i>She's bleeding badly.</i>

1192
01:25:58,072 --> 01:25:59,657
<i>We're taking her to the hospital. Over.</i>

1193
01:26:00,365 --> 01:26:01,758
<i>Message is clear. Over.</i>

1194
01:26:46,410 --> 01:26:48,203
<i>Control P13 Mobile calling.</i>

1195
01:26:48,910 --> 01:26:50,201
<i>Control answering.</i>

1196
01:26:50,398 --> 01:26:53,003
<i>Sir, the girl who was hit by the train
was taken to the hospital.</i>

1197
01:26:53,004 --> 01:26:54,318
<i>But she passed away.</i>

1198
01:26:56,635 --> 01:26:58,132
<i>She's been identified.</i>

1199
01:26:58,133 --> 01:26:59,450
<i>Her name is Keerthana.</i>

1200
01:27:49,892 --> 01:27:50,899
Shelly...

1201
01:27:51,199 --> 01:27:52,299
What's wrong?

1202
01:27:53,183 --> 01:27:54,190
Shelly!

1203
01:27:54,477 --> 01:27:55,562
What happened?

1204
01:27:56,344 --> 01:27:57,397
Go away...

1205
01:27:58,219 --> 01:27:59,385
Shelly... It's me...

1206
01:27:59,386 --> 01:28:00,407
Don't touch me!

1207
01:28:00,658 --> 01:28:01,705
Go!

1208
01:28:06,996 --> 01:28:07,999
Go!

1209
01:28:17,981 --> 01:28:19,296
Shelly...

1210
01:28:25,919 --> 01:28:27,209
- Mom...
- Shelly...

1211
01:28:27,210 --> 01:28:28,403
Mom...

1212
01:28:29,663 --> 01:28:31,879
- Dad...
- Mom!

1213
01:28:31,880 --> 01:28:32,929
Mom...

1214
01:28:33,139 --> 01:28:34,716
- It's nothing...
- Mom...

1215
01:28:34,815 --> 01:28:36,015
- Mom...
<i>- Soumya.</i>

1216
01:28:37,678 --> 01:28:38,761
<i>Open the door, Soumya.</i>

1217
01:28:38,762 --> 01:28:40,015
<i>Open up...</i>

1218
01:28:40,016 --> 01:28:41,572
- What happened?
- Mom...

1219
01:28:41,573 --> 01:28:43,312
I think he had a bad dream and got scared.

1220
01:28:47,284 --> 01:28:48,343
Shelly...

1221
01:28:54,696 --> 01:28:55,769
Shelly...

1222
01:29:01,736 --> 01:29:02,836
Shelly...

1223
01:29:20,266 --> 01:29:21,348
Hold out your hands.

1224
01:29:30,291 --> 01:29:32,622
Some things that happen in real life

1225
01:29:32,880 --> 01:29:34,079
can leave us deeply stressed.

1226
01:29:34,840 --> 01:29:37,260
And the dissonance
that comes from unanswered questions...

1227
01:29:37,700 --> 01:29:39,173
the mind struggles to accept it.

1228
01:29:39,960 --> 01:29:42,293
It won't settle until it finds a solution.

1229
01:29:44,514 --> 01:29:46,293
When you drift away from the real world

1230
01:29:46,294 --> 01:29:48,016
and move through dreams,

1231
01:29:48,017 --> 01:29:50,411
the mind starts trying
to make sense of it all.

1232
01:29:52,254 --> 01:29:55,535
This is a state bordering on delusion.

1233
01:29:57,311 --> 01:29:58,558
I'll go get the medicine.

1234
01:29:59,507 --> 01:30:00,498
Shelly...

1235
01:30:00,499 --> 01:30:02,263
<i>- When he wakes from the dream,</i>
- Shelly...

1236
01:30:02,264 --> 01:30:04,782
<i>the separation between
what's real and unreal...</i>

1237
01:30:04,783 --> 01:30:06,215
<i>becomes hard to tell apart.</i>

1238
01:30:07,660 --> 01:30:10,905
<i>It can feel like
the frightening moments from the dream</i>

1239
01:30:10,906 --> 01:30:12,640
<i>are happening in real life too.</i>

1240
01:30:13,927 --> 01:30:15,442
<i>If we don't control this now,</i>

1241
01:30:15,594 --> 01:30:17,222
<i>it could progress further.</i>

1242
01:30:20,761 --> 01:30:22,360
I've taken two days off.

1243
01:30:22,907 --> 01:30:24,533
Shall we go somewhere with the kids?

1244
01:30:28,830 --> 01:30:30,074
<i>Take the medicine regularly.</i>

1245
01:30:30,723 --> 01:30:33,544
<i>And the relaxation techniques
I told you about...</i>

1246
01:30:33,545 --> 01:30:34,995
<i>Be sure to practise them regularly.</i>

1247
01:30:34,996 --> 01:30:37,269
<i>We can slowly overcome this condition.</i>

1248
01:30:56,159 --> 01:30:57,165
Here.

1249
01:31:05,627 --> 01:31:07,280
It's getting late. I'll go get the kids.

1250
01:31:19,630 --> 01:31:21,070
What happened?

1251
01:31:21,813 --> 01:31:23,332
There was a lizard in it.

1252
01:31:24,801 --> 01:31:25,985
- Lizard?
- Yeah...

1253
01:31:25,986 --> 01:31:27,943
There wasn't anything in it
when I brought it.

1254
01:31:36,692 --> 01:31:38,637
Are you saying I imagined it?

1255
01:31:39,939 --> 01:31:41,290
That's not what I meant.

1256
01:31:41,687 --> 01:31:43,297
Isn't that what the doctor said too?

1257
01:31:43,726 --> 01:31:45,472
That's why he prescribed these medicines.

1258
01:31:46,294 --> 01:31:48,120
Are you saying I'm crazy?

1259
01:31:55,012 --> 01:31:56,515
There was a lizard in it.

1260
01:31:57,522 --> 01:31:59,402
This isn't what the doctor
was talking about.

1261
01:31:59,967 --> 01:32:01,340
Everyone at that station...

1262
01:32:01,794 --> 01:32:03,173
went through the same thing.

1263
01:32:04,853 --> 01:32:06,538
That dead girl's spirit...

1264
01:32:07,346 --> 01:32:09,906
is trying to tell me something
through that lizard.

1265
01:32:12,288 --> 01:32:14,035
This won't change with medicine alone.

1266
01:32:15,673 --> 01:32:17,367
This isn't about the film.

1267
01:32:18,573 --> 01:32:20,736
I need to know what happened to that girl.

1268
01:32:22,446 --> 01:32:24,366
Only then will I have peace.

1269
01:34:13,854 --> 01:34:15,339
I'll call you back, okay?

1270
01:34:15,889 --> 01:34:17,553
- What's it?
- A girl named Keerthana...

1271
01:34:17,554 --> 01:34:19,733
she was found dead on the tracks
around six years ago.

1272
01:34:19,734 --> 01:34:20,923
Her family lived here, right?

1273
01:34:20,924 --> 01:34:22,045
Which house was theirs?

1274
01:34:22,046 --> 01:34:23,634
That's the house, sir.

1275
01:34:23,803 --> 01:34:25,752
We bought that land from them.

1276
01:34:26,189 --> 01:34:28,169
They're in Coimbatore now.

1277
01:34:30,076 --> 01:34:31,655
Do you have their details?

1278
01:34:58,038 --> 01:34:59,890
Sir, smoking isn't allowed here.

1279
01:35:06,696 --> 01:35:08,420
She had a boyfriend.

1280
01:35:08,870 --> 01:35:10,834
She'd gone to his birthday party that day.

1281
01:35:10,991 --> 01:35:12,790
She'd told us she'd be late.

1282
01:35:12,949 --> 01:35:14,644
So we assumed her phone was switched off.

1283
01:35:14,894 --> 01:35:20,276
<i>♪ Do the shadowed forests deepen ♪</i>

1284
01:35:20,558 --> 01:35:24,292
<i>♪ Along these lonely woodland trails? ♪</i>

1285
01:35:24,496 --> 01:35:30,636
<i>♪ Where twisted trails of lies
and countless borders meet ♪</i>

1286
01:35:31,105 --> 01:35:33,785
<i>♪ In the heart of the unknown ♪</i>

1287
01:35:34,097 --> 01:35:39,402
<i>♪ Are you still searching
For the fabled golden deer ♪</i>

1288
01:35:39,816 --> 01:35:43,165
<i>♪ That wanders through
the forests of dreams?♪</i>

1289
01:35:43,707 --> 01:35:47,930
<i>♪ As your gaze reaches
into distant horizons ♪</i>

1290
01:35:47,931 --> 01:35:52,988
<i>♪ She slips away, that doe-eyed beauty! ♪</i>

1291
01:35:54,313 --> 01:35:55,834
Bro, is this the girl?

1292
01:35:56,748 --> 01:35:58,280
Where is he?

1293
01:35:58,281 --> 01:36:02,141
<i>♪ To weave the verses
Of stories still untold ♪</i>

1294
01:36:04,070 --> 01:36:05,413
Come on, let's go.

1295
01:36:06,766 --> 01:36:08,047
Sir...

1296
01:36:09,488 --> 01:36:12,777
<i>♪ Like never before ♪</i>

1297
01:36:13,300 --> 01:36:15,340
He was a member of Kaali's gang.

1298
01:36:15,909 --> 01:36:18,690
People say he ran off
with the gang leader's money.

1299
01:36:22,715 --> 01:36:24,629
Something must've happened to him, sir.

1300
01:36:24,722 --> 01:36:27,340
If he were alive,
he'd have called me at least once.

1301
01:36:40,933 --> 01:36:44,730
<i>♪ Where have your footsteps led? ♪</i>

1302
01:36:45,777 --> 01:36:48,652
<i>♪ Where does your spirit dwell? ♪</i>

1303
01:36:48,846 --> 01:36:54,165
<i>♪ When truth breaks through
All emptiness falls away ♪</i>

1304
01:36:55,386 --> 01:36:58,151
<i>♪ White waves of light arise ♪</i>

1305
01:36:58,152 --> 01:37:00,362
Where are you?
Why aren't you answering your phone?

1306
01:37:00,941 --> 01:37:03,230
<i>♪ Is this a dream in motion ♪</i>

1307
01:37:03,340 --> 01:37:07,090
<i>♪ Or a mysterious command
decreed by nature? ♪</i>

1308
01:37:07,254 --> 01:37:13,215
<i>♪ To weave the verses ♪</i>

1309
01:37:13,216 --> 01:37:16,605
<i>♪ Of stories still untold ♪</i>

1310
01:37:16,761 --> 01:37:22,707
<i>♪ To lose yourself ♪
♪ In an ecstasy ♪</i>

1311
01:37:23,597 --> 01:37:26,652
<i>♪ Like never before ♪</i>

1312
01:37:26,832 --> 01:37:32,253
<i>♪ Do the shadowed forests deepen ♪</i>

1313
01:37:32,457 --> 01:37:36,362
<i>♪ Along these lonely woodland trails? ♪</i>

1314
01:37:36,542 --> 01:37:42,307
<i>♪ Where twisted trails of lies
and countless borders meet ♪</i>

1315
01:37:42,940 --> 01:37:44,182
Hey, is your dad up?

1316
01:37:44,379 --> 01:37:45,746
- Is Dad up?
- Dad?

1317
01:37:46,604 --> 01:37:50,085
Tomorrow morning at 11 sharp,
I'll be at your office.

1318
01:37:50,569 --> 01:37:52,811
I want ten lakh rupees.

1319
01:37:53,611 --> 01:37:56,481
Otherwise, every piece of evidence I have

1320
01:37:56,938 --> 01:37:59,267
will go straight to the media
and the court.

1321
01:38:42,893 --> 01:38:44,316
Didn't I tell you?

1322
01:38:44,602 --> 01:38:47,480
That girl's spirit
was trying to tell me something.

1323
01:38:48,796 --> 01:38:50,173
Not just her.

1324
01:38:51,124 --> 01:38:53,040
Three more people were murdered.

1325
01:38:54,629 --> 01:38:56,010
This isn't just a hunch.

1326
01:38:56,185 --> 01:38:57,433
Believe me now, at least.

1327
01:38:58,961 --> 01:39:00,510
Haven't you seen the news?

1328
01:39:00,847 --> 01:39:02,312
About the land mafia?

1329
01:39:02,547 --> 01:39:04,101
They're behind all this.

1330
01:39:06,776 --> 01:39:09,307
When I went to Coimbatore
to investigate Keerthana's case,

1331
01:39:09,308 --> 01:39:10,682
the girl who died,

1332
01:39:10,840 --> 01:39:13,105
I found out she had a boyfriend there.

1333
01:39:13,106 --> 01:39:14,342
A guy named Mahesh.

1334
01:39:15,259 --> 01:39:17,040
When I started looking into him,

1335
01:39:17,041 --> 01:39:21,040
his friend told me that on the very day
Keerthana was murdered,

1336
01:39:21,525 --> 01:39:24,189
Mahesh and his Malayali grandparents
went missing.

1337
01:39:26,345 --> 01:39:27,947
He's from Palakkad, sir.

1338
01:39:28,309 --> 01:39:30,588
But he's lived here all his life, sir.

1339
01:39:31,517 --> 01:39:33,212
His grandparents were all he had.

1340
01:39:33,683 --> 01:39:36,658
No one knows where they went
after he disappeared, sir.

1341
01:39:39,163 --> 01:39:42,193
Keerthana would leave work,
travel from the textile shop to Coimbatore

1342
01:39:42,194 --> 01:39:43,889
and take the train home from there.

1343
01:39:43,890 --> 01:39:46,049
But according to Cyber Cell records,

1344
01:39:46,151 --> 01:39:47,378
on the day she died,

1345
01:39:47,379 --> 01:39:51,025
she and her boyfriend Mahesh
went to a Formiq Group construction site.

1346
01:40:12,574 --> 01:40:13,925
What happened?

1347
01:40:14,852 --> 01:40:16,183
Nothing.

1348
01:40:16,740 --> 01:40:18,879
My grandfather owns a small piece
of land in Palakkad.

1349
01:40:19,042 --> 01:40:21,829
A new party wants to buy it.

1350
01:40:22,197 --> 01:40:26,199
Once that's done, Grandpa and I
will come to your house

1351
01:40:26,668 --> 01:40:28,035
and ask for your hand.

1352
01:40:30,029 --> 01:40:32,069
They're calling me to sign some papers.

1353
01:40:32,269 --> 01:40:34,629
After that, I'll drop you at the station.

1354
01:40:44,901 --> 01:40:47,722
That's where his phone
was last switched off.

1355
01:40:48,830 --> 01:40:51,738
From there, she took a bus to Palakkad

1356
01:40:52,431 --> 01:40:55,746
and later an auto-rickshaw
to Palakkad Railway Station.

1357
01:40:56,668 --> 01:40:59,026
That day, a few men followed her
from Coimbatore

1358
01:40:59,027 --> 01:41:01,604
all the way to Palakkad Railway Station.

1359
01:41:02,599 --> 01:41:04,590
Later, Keerthana was found

1360
01:41:04,591 --> 01:41:07,471
injured near the railway tracks
close to her house.

1361
01:41:08,269 --> 01:41:11,347
It all began with the three-and-a-half-acre
plot in Meenakshipuram

1362
01:41:11,348 --> 01:41:14,041
that was in Mahesh's grandfather
Padmanabhan Nair's name.

1363
01:41:14,042 --> 01:41:16,032
His family had no idea it even existed.

1364
01:41:16,033 --> 01:41:18,030
A builders' group that bought
the adjoining land

1365
01:41:18,031 --> 01:41:20,508
discovered the property and its legal heirs

1366
01:41:20,509 --> 01:41:22,953
while processing land records
at the village office.

1367
01:41:23,298 --> 01:41:25,671
This is the notice
the Village Office sent

1368
01:41:25,672 --> 01:41:28,172
to inform the legal heirs about it.

1369
01:41:32,658 --> 01:41:36,010
The adjoining land had been bought
by a builders' group.

1370
01:41:36,011 --> 01:41:37,457
When we surveyed it,

1371
01:41:37,458 --> 01:41:39,839
we found
more land than what was listed in the deed.

1372
01:41:40,272 --> 01:41:41,916
To regularize the records,

1373
01:41:41,917 --> 01:41:45,118
they needed consent
from the adjoining landowners.

1374
01:41:46,015 --> 01:41:48,249
This is the notice sent
to the current heirs

1375
01:41:48,250 --> 01:41:50,402
informing them about it.

1376
01:41:52,299 --> 01:41:53,534
Did the heirs come here?

1377
01:41:53,683 --> 01:41:54,762
No, sir.

1378
01:41:54,763 --> 01:41:56,042
Right after sending the notice,

1379
01:41:56,043 --> 01:41:58,370
the company bought
Padmanabhan Nair's 3.5 acres too

1380
01:41:58,371 --> 01:41:59,917
and completed the transfer.

1381
01:42:00,115 --> 01:42:02,587
Padmanabhan Nair had no idea about
of his ancestral property.

1382
01:42:02,588 --> 01:42:05,589
Formiq, a builders' group, seized it
using forged documents.

1383
01:42:05,986 --> 01:42:09,626
None of the money from the land deal
ever reached his bank account.

1384
01:42:09,900 --> 01:42:11,798
Four or five days after he got the notice,

1385
01:42:12,095 --> 01:42:15,087
the entire family disappeared
without a trace.

1386
01:42:22,950 --> 01:42:25,269
Cyber Cell phone records showed

1387
01:42:25,419 --> 01:42:27,833
that Keerthana was at the same location

1388
01:42:27,834 --> 01:42:31,012
where Mahesh's and his grandfather's phones
were last switched off.

1389
01:42:32,628 --> 01:42:34,909
At Formiq Builders' construction site.

1390
01:42:36,011 --> 01:42:37,660
When you connect all the dots,

1391
01:42:38,503 --> 01:42:39,933
what happened that day...

1392
01:45:13,847 --> 01:45:15,245
Hey, stop!

1393
01:45:15,456 --> 01:45:16,651
Hey...

1394
01:45:54,207 --> 01:45:55,566
You two, follow her.

1395
01:46:19,029 --> 01:46:20,225
Hey...

1396
01:46:28,714 --> 01:46:29,951
- Palakkad.
- Where?

1397
01:46:29,952 --> 01:46:31,326
Palakkad?

1398
01:46:50,532 --> 01:46:52,226
Take the vehicle to the bus stand.

1399
01:47:58,727 --> 01:48:00,650
Watch where you're going!
Are you blind?

1400
01:48:00,737 --> 01:48:02,317
- Sorry.
- Bloody brat!

1401
01:48:02,318 --> 01:48:04,254
To Town Railway Station

1402
01:48:15,102 --> 01:48:16,873
Please, hurry!

1403
01:48:25,825 --> 01:48:27,310
Faster! Go faster!

1404
01:49:14,056 --> 01:49:15,948
This is the ladies' compartment.

1405
01:49:16,206 --> 01:49:17,431
Go sit over there.

1406
01:49:21,229 --> 01:49:22,777
Wait till the train stops.

1407
01:49:22,778 --> 01:49:24,347
We'll grab her then.

1408
01:49:24,924 --> 01:49:26,241
Just wait.

1409
01:50:32,972 --> 01:50:34,386
Drag her over here!

1410
01:50:41,573 --> 01:50:42,862
Put her there.

1411
01:50:44,509 --> 01:50:45,736
Sit there, you!

1412
01:50:45,879 --> 01:50:47,262
Sit.

1413
01:51:22,501 --> 01:51:25,135
But this case was closed
six years ago, right?

1414
01:51:25,221 --> 01:51:26,602
How are we going to prove it now?

1415
01:51:27,503 --> 01:51:29,018
Weren't you the one who said

1416
01:51:29,019 --> 01:51:31,876
everyone who looked into this
ended up in trouble?

1417
01:51:32,392 --> 01:51:35,338
If we present evidence in court
that this crime was committed,

1418
01:51:35,843 --> 01:51:37,946
the court itself will reopen the case.

1419
01:51:38,169 --> 01:51:39,511
Just wait and see.

1420
01:51:39,512 --> 01:51:42,706
By 11 tomorrow,
the evidence will be in my hands.

1421
01:51:58,038 --> 01:51:59,458
- Tell me, Bobby.
<i>- John...</i>

1422
01:51:59,871 --> 01:52:02,537
Take it up only if you can
handle it properly.

1423
01:52:02,905 --> 01:52:04,358
Otherwise, I'll handle it myself.

1424
01:52:04,359 --> 01:52:06,158
Bobby, don't do anything rash.

1425
01:52:06,638 --> 01:52:08,210
Just find out what evidence he has.

1426
01:52:08,211 --> 01:52:09,487
<i>That's all we need.</i>

1427
01:52:10,284 --> 01:52:11,751
I'm looking into him as well.

1428
01:52:12,911 --> 01:52:14,114
Just remember one thing.

1429
01:52:14,417 --> 01:52:16,829
Even a suspended cop is still a cop.

1430
01:52:36,215 --> 01:52:37,827
What evidence do you have?

1431
01:52:43,872 --> 01:52:45,759
The originals are safe with me.

1432
01:52:45,934 --> 01:52:47,195
If anything happens to me...

1433
01:52:48,686 --> 01:52:49,939
all of this will go public.

1434
01:52:52,561 --> 01:52:53,568
So, can I take this?

1435
01:53:25,135 --> 01:53:26,623
<i>Over there... Come...</i>

1436
01:53:26,624 --> 01:53:28,448
Sir... please listen to me.

1437
01:53:28,449 --> 01:53:29,542
Please cooperate.

1438
01:53:29,543 --> 01:53:31,138
I didn't come here to blackmail anyone.

1439
01:53:31,521 --> 01:53:33,478
Sir, I came here to collect
evidence for a case.

1440
01:53:33,479 --> 01:53:35,063
Sir... Please listen to me.

1441
01:53:35,306 --> 01:53:36,693
Sir, please don't do this.

1442
01:53:36,694 --> 01:53:38,112
I've got evidence against them...

1443
01:53:38,319 --> 01:53:39,558
Sir, please listen to me...

1444
01:53:39,559 --> 01:53:40,864
Please don't do this, sir...

1445
01:53:40,865 --> 01:53:42,885
Sir... please just listen...
Let me go.

1446
01:53:43,911 --> 01:53:45,321
I didn't do anything wrong.

1447
01:53:45,322 --> 01:53:47,101
I came here only to collect evidence...

1448
01:53:47,102 --> 01:53:49,026
<i>A suspended police officer
has been arrested</i>

1449
01:53:49,027 --> 01:53:50,864
<i>by the Vigilance Department
in a bribery case.</i>

1450
01:53:50,960 --> 01:53:53,712
<i>Shelly, a Civil Police Officer
attached to Kongad Police Station,</i>

1451
01:53:53,713 --> 01:53:55,559
<i>was taken into custody
by the Vigilance team.</i>

1452
01:53:55,560 --> 01:53:59,733
<i>These are visuals of Shelly being
taken to the Palakkad Vigilance Office</i>

1453
01:53:59,955 --> 01:54:01,388
<i>for further questioning.</i>

1454
01:54:01,481 --> 01:54:03,232
<i>After being caught in the Vigilance trap,</i>

1455
01:54:03,233 --> 01:54:05,285
<i>Shelly was forcibly detained by the team.</i>

1456
01:54:05,286 --> 01:54:08,676
<i>Vigilance acted on
confidential information that</i>

1457
01:54:08,677 --> 01:54:11,196
<i>Shelly had demanded a bribe from builders.</i>

1458
01:54:11,355 --> 01:54:13,299
<i>The trap was laid following a complaint</i>

1459
01:54:13,300 --> 01:54:15,840
<i>filed by Bobby Kurian, MD of Formiq Group.</i>

1460
01:54:30,809 --> 01:54:33,047
The footage just shown
before this Hon'ble Court

1461
01:54:33,048 --> 01:54:35,188
was recorded by my client
using a pen camera.

1462
01:54:35,874 --> 01:54:38,208
The purpose of this sting operation was

1463
01:54:38,473 --> 01:54:41,323
to investigate Keerthana's death
that occurred six years ago

1464
01:54:41,461 --> 01:54:43,745
and establish before this Court that

1465
01:54:43,746 --> 01:54:45,913
it was not an accident, but a murder.

1466
01:54:46,374 --> 01:54:48,026
My client sought money from the builders

1467
01:54:48,145 --> 01:54:50,486
only to gather evidence for that purpose.

1468
01:54:50,698 --> 01:54:52,965
Considering my client's
bona fide intentions,

1469
01:54:53,063 --> 01:54:55,750
I humbly request that he be acquitted.

1470
01:54:56,298 --> 01:54:57,443
Objection, Your Honour.

1471
01:54:58,831 --> 01:55:00,897
The accused fabricated a murder case

1472
01:55:00,898 --> 01:55:03,064
to blackmail a company and extort money.

1473
01:55:03,263 --> 01:55:05,279
That was his sole intention.

1474
01:55:06,057 --> 01:55:07,363
In case he ever got caught,

1475
01:55:07,364 --> 01:55:10,096
this so-called sting operation
was his escape plan.

1476
01:55:10,691 --> 01:55:12,337
The accused is no ordinary person.

1477
01:55:12,338 --> 01:55:15,343
The Court must bear in mind
that he is a police officer

1478
01:55:15,344 --> 01:55:17,605
well-versed in the law and its loopholes.

1479
01:55:17,778 --> 01:55:19,244
What made you believe

1480
01:55:19,245 --> 01:55:21,298
Keerthana's death was a murder?

1481
01:55:21,578 --> 01:55:23,855
Three acres of land
belonging to Padmanabhan Nair

1482
01:55:24,076 --> 01:55:26,372
were acquired by this company
using forged documents.

1483
01:55:26,511 --> 01:55:28,909
When Padmanabhan Nair, his wife,

1484
01:55:29,031 --> 01:55:30,310
and their grandson Mahesh

1485
01:55:30,458 --> 01:55:32,024
started looking into the land scam,

1486
01:55:32,025 --> 01:55:33,454
the company had them killed.

1487
01:55:33,618 --> 01:55:36,238
Keerthana, who witnessed the crime,
was also murdered.

1488
01:55:36,651 --> 01:55:38,628
They made her death look like an accident.

1489
01:55:41,344 --> 01:55:42,378
Your Honour,

1490
01:55:42,578 --> 01:55:44,848
if the Hon'ble Court examines these deeds,

1491
01:55:44,849 --> 01:55:47,257
it will be clear that his claims
are purely speculative.

1492
01:55:47,639 --> 01:55:49,223
The company lawfully purchased the land

1493
01:55:49,224 --> 01:55:51,240
after paying the amount
stated in these documents.

1494
01:55:51,351 --> 01:55:53,734
This is Padmanabhan Nair's bank passbook.

1495
01:55:54,336 --> 01:55:56,044
A review of these records will show

1496
01:55:56,045 --> 01:55:58,896
that none of the money in question
was ever credited to Nair's account.

1497
01:55:59,634 --> 01:56:01,803
As Nair was facing bank attachment

1498
01:56:01,804 --> 01:56:03,737
after defaulting on a loan,

1499
01:56:03,828 --> 01:56:05,348
he received the money through

1500
01:56:05,434 --> 01:56:06,973
his grandson Mahesh's account

1501
01:56:06,974 --> 01:56:08,796
to prevent it from being seized.

1502
01:56:15,648 --> 01:56:17,634
They've fabricated these documents.

1503
01:56:19,390 --> 01:56:21,679
If the Court orders an investigation
by a central agency,

1504
01:56:21,680 --> 01:56:22,902
it will reveal the truth.

1505
01:56:24,857 --> 01:56:26,253
It wasn't just one murder.

1506
01:56:26,425 --> 01:56:27,644
Including Keerthana,

1507
01:56:27,645 --> 01:56:28,845
there were four victims.

1508
01:56:31,245 --> 01:56:32,766
Only when everyone responsible

1509
01:56:33,384 --> 01:56:35,024
is brought to justice

1510
01:56:35,245 --> 01:56:37,141
will that girl's soul find peace.

1511
01:56:42,678 --> 01:56:45,844
This Court believes the matter should
be considered by the Magistrate Court.

1512
01:56:46,062 --> 01:56:47,456
So, we shall transfer it.

1513
01:56:47,578 --> 01:56:49,684
If this Hon'ble Court transfers the case

1514
01:56:49,685 --> 01:56:51,416
based on mere speculation,

1515
01:56:51,417 --> 01:56:53,263
the company will suffer huge losses

1516
01:56:53,264 --> 01:56:55,270
on its upcoming housing projects,

1517
01:56:55,271 --> 01:56:57,612
including crores in investments
and its goodwill.

1518
01:56:57,971 --> 01:56:59,003
I humbly request

1519
01:56:59,004 --> 01:57:00,833
the Court for a little more time.

1520
01:57:01,125 --> 01:57:04,296
The company has filed a habeas corpus
petition before the Coimbatore Court

1521
01:57:04,455 --> 01:57:06,657
to trace the missing
Padmanabhan Nair and his family.

1522
01:57:07,051 --> 01:57:09,787
I request permission
to question the accused.

1523
01:57:09,788 --> 01:57:10,794
Please proceed.

1524
01:57:12,281 --> 01:57:13,669
How did you investigate

1525
01:57:13,828 --> 01:57:15,488
and uncover these alleged murders?

1526
01:57:18,587 --> 01:57:19,594
Tell me.

1527
01:57:20,067 --> 01:57:22,220
It was Keerthana's soul,
still seeking justice,

1528
01:57:22,513 --> 01:57:24,273
that led me to these murders.

1529
01:57:24,378 --> 01:57:25,385
Oh...

1530
01:57:25,786 --> 01:57:27,157
So it was the dead girl's spirit

1531
01:57:27,158 --> 01:57:28,405
that guided you?

1532
01:57:31,043 --> 01:57:32,050
That's fascinating.

1533
01:57:32,350 --> 01:57:34,749
A former Chief Justice once claimed

1534
01:57:35,452 --> 01:57:37,369
he spoke to his late wife's spirit.

1535
01:57:37,370 --> 01:57:38,431
Is that so?

1536
01:57:38,432 --> 01:57:39,572
Do you doubt that?

1537
01:57:39,658 --> 01:57:40,664
No.

1538
01:57:41,498 --> 01:57:43,203
A dead girl's spirit

1539
01:57:43,204 --> 01:57:44,591
summoned by a tantric,

1540
01:57:44,944 --> 01:57:46,178
helped solve a case.

1541
01:57:46,344 --> 01:57:47,657
A former DGP said so.

1542
01:57:47,791 --> 01:57:49,384
- Oh, really?
- Do you doubt that too?

1543
01:57:49,471 --> 01:57:50,478
Not at all.

1544
01:57:51,585 --> 01:57:54,049
The soul of a girl
who was wrongfully killed

1545
01:57:54,050 --> 01:57:55,451
is seeking justice here.

1546
01:57:56,251 --> 01:57:58,213
The Court must order an investigation.

1547
01:57:58,415 --> 01:57:59,447
Okay, okay.

1548
01:57:59,448 --> 01:58:01,300
I humbly request permission

1549
01:58:01,301 --> 01:58:03,160
to examine one more witness.

1550
01:58:03,362 --> 01:58:04,368
Yes, proceed.

1551
01:58:13,845 --> 01:58:15,424
Is he your patient, Doctor?

1552
01:58:16,438 --> 01:58:17,445
Yes.

1553
01:58:17,784 --> 01:58:19,977
Shelly has been my patient
for the past four years.

1554
01:58:20,624 --> 01:58:23,764
What condition was he receiving
treatment for?

1555
01:58:24,751 --> 01:58:27,276
Because of the many
extramarital affair cases

1556
01:58:27,277 --> 01:58:29,341
he encountered in police work,

1557
01:58:29,977 --> 01:58:33,064
he began to suspect
his wife was having one too.

1558
01:58:33,577 --> 01:58:35,616
That suspicion gradually became a delusion.

1559
01:58:35,711 --> 01:58:37,251
The death of his father,

1560
01:58:37,390 --> 01:58:39,420
the pressure of writing scripts

1561
01:58:39,521 --> 01:58:41,043
and dealing with their failures,

1562
01:58:41,044 --> 01:58:42,457
worsened his delusional disorder,

1563
01:58:42,458 --> 01:58:44,943
eventually leading to
paranoid schizophrenia.

1564
01:58:44,944 --> 01:58:46,162
Your Honour...

1565
01:58:46,163 --> 01:58:47,170
Please believe me.

1566
01:58:49,681 --> 01:58:51,631
They're trying to portray me
as mentally ill

1567
01:58:51,632 --> 01:58:53,346
so this case won't be reopened.

1568
01:58:55,968 --> 01:58:58,474
That's why they've paid this doctor
to testify against me.

1569
01:59:01,931 --> 01:59:03,729
What's more important?
The company's goodwill

1570
01:59:03,730 --> 01:59:05,051
or the lives of four people?

1571
01:59:08,861 --> 01:59:10,534
Those innocent people deserve justice.

1572
01:59:11,507 --> 01:59:12,513
Please...

1573
01:59:12,715 --> 01:59:13,788
Shelly.

1574
01:59:15,087 --> 01:59:17,246
What exactly is paranoid schizophrenia,
Doctor?

1575
01:59:17,247 --> 01:59:18,527
Can you explain it in detail?

1576
01:59:18,874 --> 01:59:21,712
A person suffering from
paranoid schizophrenia

1577
01:59:21,713 --> 01:59:24,739
may lose touch with reality
and become trapped in their delusions.

1578
01:59:25,488 --> 01:59:28,521
They begin to live
within that imagined reality.

1579
01:59:29,021 --> 01:59:30,985
They may also experience
auditory hallucinations,

1580
01:59:30,986 --> 01:59:32,794
hearing voices that others cannot hear.

1581
01:59:33,115 --> 01:59:35,386
They may see things that do not exist

1582
01:59:35,387 --> 01:59:37,895
and feel as though those experiences
are happening to them.

1583
01:59:38,041 --> 01:59:40,947
Their thoughts and actions eventually
revolve around those delusions.

1584
01:59:40,948 --> 01:59:41,955
That's all, Your Honour.

1585
01:59:44,248 --> 01:59:46,452
It is unlawful for a person
of unsound mental health

1586
01:59:46,453 --> 01:59:48,439
to continue in the police force.

1587
01:59:48,620 --> 01:59:51,973
Therefore, the Court directs
the District Superintendent of Police

1588
01:59:51,974 --> 01:59:54,746
to have the accused medically examined
and submit a report.

1589
01:59:55,048 --> 01:59:56,055
Thank you, Your Honour.

1590
02:00:00,090 --> 02:00:01,606
If you brand me as crazy...

1591
02:00:01,607 --> 02:00:03,570
the truth behind four murders
will never come out.

1592
02:00:03,743 --> 02:00:05,347
- Shelly!
- Stop it. This is a courtroom.

1593
02:00:05,348 --> 02:00:07,301
- Don't think you can call me crazy...
- Shelly...

1594
02:00:07,302 --> 02:00:08,882
- and get away with this case!
- Silence!

1595
02:00:08,883 --> 02:00:11,386
I don't care what the court says
or if you lock me up...

1596
02:00:11,387 --> 02:00:13,785
The accused is remanded
for 14 days for medical examination.

1597
02:00:13,786 --> 02:00:15,507
The case is adjourned to the next hearing.

1598
02:00:15,508 --> 02:00:16,538
Handcuff him.

1599
02:00:16,539 --> 02:00:18,640
- I won't let any of you get away with this.
- Lock it.

1600
02:00:18,773 --> 02:00:20,860
- I'll make sure all of you go to jail.
- Shelly

1601
02:00:20,861 --> 02:00:22,354
- Calm down, Shelly.
- I have proof...

1602
02:00:22,355 --> 02:00:24,380
- Stay still.
- I'm not crazy!

1603
02:00:24,954 --> 02:00:26,422
I'm not crazy...

1604
02:00:26,423 --> 02:00:27,703
Please believe me.

1605
02:00:28,128 --> 02:00:29,674
I'm not crazy...

1606
02:00:30,630 --> 02:00:32,037
- Shelly, stay still.
- Let me go!

1607
02:00:32,038 --> 02:00:33,202
Don't fight back.

1608
02:00:33,203 --> 02:00:34,996
They can't brand me crazy

1609
02:00:34,997 --> 02:00:36,370
and make this case go away.

1610
02:00:36,371 --> 02:00:37,461
Shelly... listen to me.

1611
02:00:37,462 --> 02:00:39,923
I'll make sure every one of them
goes to prison. Let me go.

1612
02:00:40,044 --> 02:00:41,075
Soumya...

1613
02:00:41,076 --> 02:00:42,206
Tell them I'm not crazy.

1614
02:00:42,207 --> 02:00:43,760
Please just tell... I'm not crazy.

1615
02:00:44,679 --> 02:00:45,759
Soumya...

1616
02:00:46,398 --> 02:00:47,471
Soumya...

1617
02:00:48,211 --> 02:00:49,285
Say I'm not crazy...

1618
02:00:52,415 --> 02:00:53,831
Please don't do this to me.

1619
02:00:53,832 --> 02:00:54,947
I...

1620
02:01:12,288 --> 02:01:13,381
Don't worry, Soumya.

1621
02:01:13,641 --> 02:01:14,648
Go back to the quarters.

1622
02:01:14,768 --> 02:01:16,141
I'll call you if there's anything.

1623
02:01:17,341 --> 02:01:19,276
There may be some truth
to what he's saying.

1624
02:01:19,277 --> 02:01:21,323
It makes no sense to bring in
a High Court lawyer

1625
02:01:21,324 --> 02:01:22,678
for a simple bribery case.

1626
02:01:25,685 --> 02:01:26,691
You can go.

1627
02:03:40,877 --> 02:03:42,183
Hey... Joshy...

1628
02:03:43,264 --> 02:03:44,777
Take these off. My hands hurt.

1629
02:03:44,778 --> 02:03:46,063
Just lie there, Shelly.

1630
02:03:46,310 --> 02:03:47,642
Let the doctor see you tomorrow.

1631
02:03:47,643 --> 02:03:48,847
You brought this on yourself.

1632
02:03:48,848 --> 02:03:50,929
Do you think I'm crazy too?

1633
02:03:52,351 --> 02:03:53,818
Then why did you do that in court?

1634
02:03:55,898 --> 02:03:57,877
If everyone was trying
to paint you as crazy,

1635
02:03:57,878 --> 02:03:59,612
what would you have done
in my place?

1636
02:04:05,350 --> 02:04:08,043
They trapped me
to stop the case from being reopened.

1637
02:04:09,658 --> 02:04:11,183
Just give me a little more time.

1638
02:04:12,365 --> 02:04:13,723
I have all the evidence.

1639
02:04:15,991 --> 02:04:17,498
Or they'll brand me as crazy,

1640
02:04:17,950 --> 02:04:18,956
and I'll lose my job.

1641
02:04:22,118 --> 02:04:24,304
I know where
those three are buried.

1642
02:04:25,845 --> 02:04:27,142
Shelly...

1643
02:04:27,409 --> 02:04:29,142
I know this will get you into trouble.

1644
02:04:32,037 --> 02:04:33,392
My life is in your hands.

1645
02:04:34,870 --> 02:04:36,536
You're the only one
who can help me.

1646
02:04:50,431 --> 02:04:51,684
It's only a Vigilance case.

1647
02:04:52,331 --> 02:04:54,064
At worst,
I'll be suspended for six months.

1648
02:04:54,917 --> 02:04:56,023
I can live with that.

1649
02:07:04,957 --> 02:07:06,098
Get up, man!

1650
02:07:07,323 --> 02:07:08,436
Stand still!

1651
02:11:56,706 --> 02:11:58,231
Sir, this is a very old case,

1652
02:11:58,232 --> 02:11:59,945
and all the victims are from Kerala.

1653
02:11:59,946 --> 02:12:01,818
Then suddenly,
the Tamil Nadu Police steps in

1654
02:12:01,819 --> 02:12:03,240
and cracks the case.

1655
02:12:03,241 --> 02:12:04,308
How did that happen, sir?

1656
02:12:04,309 --> 02:12:05,969
Did you receive any secret information?

1657
02:12:06,645 --> 02:12:07,680
Nothing like that.

1658
02:12:07,681 --> 02:12:10,100
It was a lead from
an ordinary policeman from Kerala

1659
02:12:10,656 --> 02:12:13,386
that helped Tamil Nadu Police
solve this case.

1660
02:12:19,786 --> 02:12:23,343
Sir, this was ruled
an accidental death years ago.

1661
02:12:23,344 --> 02:12:25,986
How did you conclude
it was linked to multiple murders

1662
02:12:25,987 --> 02:12:28,590
and that this is where
the bodies were buried?

1663
02:12:30,553 --> 02:12:31,898
She brought me here.

1664
02:12:32,554 --> 02:12:34,099
The spirit of the girl who died.

1665
02:13:09,284 --> 02:13:10,364
Cut.

1666
02:13:20,818 --> 02:13:22,562
- Thank you.
- If you'd like a place to write,

1667
02:13:22,563 --> 02:13:23,684
we have a property in Dubai.

1668
02:13:23,802 --> 02:13:24,913
And one in Wayanad as well.

1669
02:13:24,914 --> 02:13:27,229
If you'd prefer somewhere else,
just let us know.

1670
02:13:33,090 --> 02:13:34,630
No, I'll stay here and write.

1671
02:13:35,170 --> 02:13:36,177
I'm comfortable here.

1672
02:13:36,611 --> 02:13:37,618
Okay.

1673
02:13:38,143 --> 02:13:39,150
Let's go?

1674
02:13:40,070 --> 02:13:41,890
It'd be great if we could get
the first draft in a month.

1675
02:13:41,891 --> 02:13:42,949
Sure.

1676
02:13:42,950 --> 02:13:43,957
Okay, then.

1677
02:14:35,811 --> 02:14:36,818
Sir.

1678
02:14:38,909 --> 02:14:40,162
I'm a new recruit, sir.

1679
02:14:44,342 --> 02:14:45,732
Are you into writing stories?

1680
02:14:46,650 --> 02:14:47,657
No, sir.

1681
02:14:48,143 --> 02:14:49,223
Mm.

1682
02:14:49,924 --> 02:14:50,930
Give it to the writer.

1683
02:14:57,277 --> 02:14:59,643
Enter your details in that biodata book.

1684
02:14:59,891 --> 02:15:00,968
Okay, sir.

1685
02:15:00,969 --> 02:15:01,996
And one more thing...

1686
02:15:02,509 --> 02:15:03,516
see that box?

1687
02:15:05,645 --> 02:15:07,275
For God's sake, please don't touch it.

1688
02:15:07,391 --> 02:15:08,534
There's a file inside.

1689
02:15:08,684 --> 02:15:09,934
The last person who touched it

1690
02:15:09,935 --> 02:15:11,511
lost both his job and his mind.